(4470026, 640553, 61961, '<td valign="top">Beautiful portrait.  I bumped this up to a 10 tonight before the voting closed.  Cool depth of field and lovely blues.  The hat is the best.  Cheers,</td>', 'Beautiful portrait.  I bumped this up to a 10 tonight before the voting closed.  Cool depth of field and lovely blues.  The hat is the best.  Cheers,', '2008-02-08 00:34:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470028, 640844, 38477, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by taterbug:</b></div><hr/><i> Great eye on this one. Very nice choice of subject. I like the centered approach for the composition, there is good symmetry here, and the single black ''s'' at top offers nice opposition, and tension in the shot, a good ''break up'' for the scene. However, it is just a little ''off'', just enough to seem careless, and not fully thought out. I think in a shot like this, it can be greatly strengthened by really nailing the symmetry present, and emphasizing and driving home the centered comp. With all the lines that are here, going right to the edge of the frame, it is easy to see that it is not ''straight'', or in line. Also, the distance from the edge of both sides of the frame, to the edge of the windows is not the same. I would say it looks like your shooting position could of been just a step or two to the left, and really squared it all up tight. I mean, this is just so close to that, it seems like that is the intent. This is just not ''off'' enought to seem like it was the chosen POV. But if it was, then ignore me :-) Still a nice shot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks all for the comments..<br/> <br/>taterbug: you are right.. a bit lazy on my part and I found lateral misalignment is tricky to correct in PP :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by taterbug: Great eye on this one. Very nice choice of subject. I like the centered approach for the composition, there is good symmetry here, and the single black ''s'' at top offers nice opposition, and tension in the shot, a good ''break up'' for the scene. However, it is just a little ''off'', just enough to seem careless, and not fully thought out. I think in a shot like this, it can be greatly strengthened by really nailing the symmetry present, and emphasizing and driving home the centered comp. With all the lines that are here, going right to the edge of the frame, it is easy to see that it is not ''straight'', or in line. Also, the distance from the edge of both sides of the frame, to the edge of the windows is not the same. I would say it looks like your shooting position could of been just a step or two to the left, and really squared it all up tight. I mean, this is just so close to that, it seems like that is the intent. This is just not ''off'' enought to seem like it was the chosen POV. But if it was, then ignore me :-) Still a nice shot.   thanks all for the comments.. taterbug: you are right.. a bit lazy on my part and I found lateral misalignment is tricky to correct in PP :-)', '2008-02-08 00:35:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470029, 640715, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised this did not place higher. Perhaps a touch more oomph in the colors would have given it that extra something, but as I said in my previous comment, I like it.</td>', 'I''m surprised this did not place higher. Perhaps a touch more oomph in the colors would have given it that extra something, but as I said in my previous comment, I like it.', '2008-02-08 00:35:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470037, 633136, 67258, '<td valign="top">A superb photo, I thought it would finish higher - I was one of your 9s.  looking forward to seeing more like this once DPL gets going again.</td>', 'A superb photo, I thought it would finish higher - I was one of your 9s.  looking forward to seeing more like this once DPL gets going again.', '2008-02-08 00:37:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470039, 640758, 83313, '<td valign="top">I have a two monitor setup, the larger one has a backlight lamp burned out and everything looks a shade darker and richer on that one. (I don''t use that one for voting because it''s inaccurate and details in shadows get lost) I actually like this shot better on the problem monitor. I would have likely scored it one notch higher if it had looked like that in voting. (I gave it a 6, BTW)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 00:40:40.</i></td>', 'I have a two monitor setup, the larger one has a backlight lamp burned out and everything looks a shade darker and richer on that one. (I don''t use that one for voting because it''s inaccurate and details in shadows get lost) I actually like this shot better on the problem monitor. I would have likely scored it one notch higher if it had looked like that in voting. (I gave it a 6, BTW)', '2008-02-08 00:39:48.000000', '2008-02-08 00:40:40.000000', 0),
(4470040, 633081, 29011, '<td valign="top">I''m glad you posted the shot. When I mentioned green cast, it''s more of a slight light cyan. Not like grass green. You got PM ;)</td>', 'I''m glad you posted the shot. When I mentioned green cast, it''s more of a slight light cyan. Not like grass green. You got PM ;)', '2008-02-08 00:40:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470042, 637910, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nice name. <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=79816" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Daryn</a> seems to have thought so as well.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=635084" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/635084.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/635084.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/635084.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 00:43:02.</i></td>', 'Nice name.  Daryn seems to have thought so as well.', '2008-02-08 00:42:39.000000', '2008-02-08 00:43:02.000000', 0),
(4470046, 640693, 67258, '<td valign="top">This was amongst my favourite of the challenge.  Your title perfectly sums up the feelings evoked by the photo. Excellent work.</td>', 'This was amongst my favourite of the challenge.  Your title perfectly sums up the feelings evoked by the photo. Excellent work.', '2008-02-08 00:47:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470049, 640490, 48697, '<td valign="top">I think the the first thing that I notice in this shot is that it has the apperance of being oof or lacking any sharpness in the mountain area.  I also feel the moon is looks pixilated.  I think that the mountain line running dead center makes the picture a bit dull, maybe cropping the top or the bottom to put it more in the thirds could help the shot. I do like the blue sky but there seems to be some banding, try to tone down the curves or the hue/saturation to minimize that issue. Landscape moon shots are somewhat difficult b/c the moon appears much bigger in person than it will ever appear in the photo unless minipulated. Trevor~</td>', 'I think the the first thing that I notice in this shot is that it has the apperance of being oof or lacking any sharpness in the mountain area.  I also feel the moon is looks pixilated.  I think that the mountain line running dead center makes the picture a bit dull, maybe cropping the top or the bottom to put it more in the thirds could help the shot. I do like the blue sky but there seems to be some banding, try to tone down the curves or the hue/saturation to minimize that issue. Landscape moon shots are somewhat difficult b/c the moon appears much bigger in person than it will ever appear in the photo unless minipulated. Trevor~', '2008-02-08 00:53:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470058, 640869, 24495, '<td valign="top">The greatest picture I have ever seen!</td>', 'The greatest picture I have ever seen!', '2008-02-08 00:56:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470063, 640490, 79955, '<td valign="top">Actually it is very well done, nice saturated colors , sharp. You were spot on when you mentioned not very exciting. Against the many landscapes &amp; seascapes , it is really tough. <br/>To improve futher I recommend that you change the composition a little include more of the sky. For the record I rated this a 6.<br/> <br/>Don''t fret, yours shots are definitely improving. My recomendations, shoot more , study the top pics in the challenge. As I have found in my participation , selecting the right shot for the challenge is a big part of whether we do well or not...</td>', 'Actually it is very well done, nice saturated colors , sharp. You were spot on when you mentioned not very exciting. Against the many landscapes & seascapes , it is really tough. To improve futher I recommend that you change the composition a little include more of the sky. For the record I rated this a 6. Don''t fret, yours shots are definitely improving. My recomendations, shoot more , study the top pics in the challenge. As I have found in my participation , selecting the right shot for the challenge is a big part of whether we do well or not...', '2008-02-08 00:57:46.000000', NULL, 0),
