(4470890, 640398, 14476, '<td valign="top">Well, Larus, you didn''t get any "1s" on this one, and if <b>this</b> was the placeholder, well what might have been would be even more fantastic.<br/> <br/>You folks have so many natural wonders in that fabulous land of yours, that if you ever entered examples of them all, you''d be on the front page every week and tourists would be flocking to Iceland.<br/>The lava flows, the waterfalls, the geysers, glaciers, calderas, and on and on, let alone the light shows you present, like this one.  <br/> <br/>Keep ''em coming.<br/></td>', 'Well, Larus, you didn''t get any "1s" on this one, and if this was the placeholder, well what might have been would be even more fantastic. You folks have so many natural wonders in that fabulous land of yours, that if you ever entered examples of them all, you''d be on the front page every week and tourists would be flocking to Iceland.The lava flows, the waterfalls, the geysers, glaciers, calderas, and on and on, let alone the light shows you present, like this one.   Keep ''em coming.', '2008-02-08 10:34:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470893, 638137, 89763, '<td valign="top">This is awesome! Perfect lighting, compo, dof, contrast - everything! I can''t believe <i>everyone</i> didn''t give this a <b>10</b>.</td>', 'This is awesome! Perfect lighting, compo, dof, contrast - everything! I can''t believe everyone didn''t give this a 10.', '2008-02-08 10:35:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470896, 640774, 67697, '<td valign="top">You know, I was sure you were from Michigan and then I was going to comment on how amazing it is that there''s no ice on the lake lol.  So I see you were lucky to have taken this in a much warmer climate :)  I loved the blue, gray, and brown tones of this shot.  Including the lone person is a nice enhancement to the mood of the scene.</td>', 'You know, I was sure you were from Michigan and then I was going to comment on how amazing it is that there''s no ice on the lake lol.  So I see you were lucky to have taken this in a much warmer climate :)  I loved the blue, gray, and brown tones of this shot.  Including the lone person is a nice enhancement to the mood of the scene.', '2008-02-08 10:36:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470901, 633427, 43073, '<td valign="top">Brilliant shot, congrats on the ribbon. It''s so nice to see my home town so well represented. Better than anything I''ve done here, and I''d bet you were only in town for the day (and why would anyone stay here longer than that?). Drop me a note next time you''re here and maybe we can share a pint.</td>', 'Brilliant shot, congrats on the ribbon. It''s so nice to see my home town so well represented. Better than anything I''ve done here, and I''d bet you were only in town for the day (and why would anyone stay here longer than that?). Drop me a note next time you''re here and maybe we can share a pint.', '2008-02-08 10:39:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470906, 639468, 40484, '<td valign="top">I like the angle of the shot. Perhaps try a closer crop that removes the road and the building on the right, leaving the group of three main buildings on the left. I would also crop the top down to just below the dotted lights over the tallest building. This gives them more impact, IMHO. To me, the sky also seems to have some artifacting happening that shows some brush strokes? Maybe a little more digital noise removal or a guassian blur to smooth that out.</td>', 'I like the angle of the shot. Perhaps try a closer crop that removes the road and the building on the right, leaving the group of three main buildings on the left. I would also crop the top down to just below the dotted lights over the tallest building. This gives them more impact, IMHO. To me, the sky also seems to have some artifacting happening that shows some brush strokes? Maybe a little more digital noise removal or a guassian blur to smooth that out.', '2008-02-08 10:43:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470907, 629830, 67697, '<td valign="top">Uh, oh, you scored above a 6 and are in the top 75 in a FS.  Hope you are feeling ok :P<br/> <br/>I think mist/fog/clouds and trees are such a beautiful and mystical combo.  I like the perspective as I get a feeling of really having to tilt my head back to look up.  I agree about the crooked branch adding some interest, because it breaks away from the stick-straight patterns of all the other trees.  Great shot.</td>', 'Uh, oh, you scored above a 6 and are in the top 75 in a FS.  Hope you are feeling ok :P I think mist/fog/clouds and trees are such a beautiful and mystical combo.  I like the perspective as I get a feeling of really having to tilt my head back to look up.  I agree about the crooked branch adding some interest, because it breaks away from the stick-straight patterns of all the other trees.  Great shot.', '2008-02-08 10:43:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470908, 633017, 39663, '<td valign="top">Total awe!!!!! My brain is actually frozen now. Thanks.</td>', 'Total awe!!!!! My brain is actually frozen now. Thanks.', '2008-02-08 10:43:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470912, 640035, 11854, '<td valign="top">I was also quite amused by this. I gave it a 7 in voting. The thought of boiled peanuts being sold with antiques is humerous in itself, but throw in that "building" and it just cracks me up.</td>', 'I was also quite amused by this. I gave it a 7 in voting. The thought of boiled peanuts being sold with antiques is humerous in itself, but throw in that "building" and it just cracks me up.', '2008-02-08 10:44:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470914, 640035, 71608, '<td valign="top">I love lots about this one! The depth-of-field is great, the clarity is great, the B+W conversion is great, the framing is great... I think it''s a photo that tells a story, and it makes me giggle :)</td>', 'I love lots about this one! The depth-of-field is great, the clarity is great, the B+W conversion is great, the framing is great... I think it''s a photo that tells a story, and it makes me giggle :)', '2008-02-08 10:45:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470916, 640211, 67697, '<td valign="top">You must have had a great time photographing animals like this.  I would love to do that some day.  I think my favorite part of this is how it looks like the horn is glowing.  It has such a beautiful and rich golden color.  I love the details you can see on it too.</td>', 'You must have had a great time photographing animals like this.  I would love to do that some day.  I think my favorite part of this is how it looks like the horn is glowing.  It has such a beautiful and rich golden color.  I love the details you can see on it too.', '2008-02-08 10:47:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470920, 638823, 11854, '<td valign="top">Very pretty, delicate, great DOF. There is some oddness going on from the infrared that I think hurt your score.</td>', 'Very pretty, delicate, great DOF. There is some oddness going on from the infrared that I think hurt your score.', '2008-02-08 10:48:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470921, 640941, 51538, '<td valign="top">I liked the lighting entering the box.  Interesting image.  Glad you put it into the challenge.</td>', 'I liked the lighting entering the box.  Interesting image.  Glad you put it into the challenge.', '2008-02-08 10:49:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470922, 639803, 67697, '<td valign="top">Well, I personally liked this shot and now that I see your original, I loooooooove the processing.  This would look perfect on a card.  I love the soft glow and also love that you used PP to enhance the textures.  Let me know when you decide to share the processing steps!</td>', 'Well, I personally liked this shot and now that I see your original, I loooooooove the processing.  This would look perfect on a card.  I love the soft glow and also love that you used PP to enhance the textures.  Let me know when you decide to share the processing steps!', '2008-02-08 10:51:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470923, 636534, 51538, '<td valign="top">Pleasant viewing experience in this challenge.  Glad you entered this photo.</td>', 'Pleasant viewing experience in this challenge.  Glad you entered this photo.', '2008-02-08 10:51:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470926, 640231, 11854, '<td valign="top">I adore how it looks like the flower on the wall is actually on her head like an extension of the barrette. The processing is beautiful. That said, tattooing (especially on women) seems to turn a lot of people off, which could account for the low score.</td>', 'I adore how it looks like the flower on the wall is actually on her head like an extension of the barrette. The processing is beautiful. That said, tattooing (especially on women) seems to turn a lot of people off, which could account for the low score.', '2008-02-08 10:51:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470927, 638137, 47205, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot! I really love the contrasts within this. Well done and congrats on the blue!!!</td>', 'Awesome shot! I really love the contrasts within this. Well done and congrats on the blue!!!', '2008-02-08 10:53:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470928, 638112, 67697, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get to finish voting so I am glad I am seeing this now.  It''s gorgeous!  I love the different color shades of the sky.  I love that the tree is arching over to fill the top of the frame.  And the streaks of light are very cool.  Great catch!</td>', 'I didn''t get to finish voting so I am glad I am seeing this now.  It''s gorgeous!  I love the different color shades of the sky.  I love that the tree is arching over to fill the top of the frame.  And the streaks of light are very cool.  Great catch!', '2008-02-08 10:54:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470929, 640398, 51538, '<td valign="top">Would be interesting to see this image on a full size basis.  The ISO and aperture you used are fairly extreme.  It must have been a rather dark night.</td>', 'Would be interesting to see this image on a full size basis.  The ISO and aperture you used are fairly extreme.  It must have been a rather dark night.', '2008-02-08 10:54:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470930, 638137, 51538, '<td valign="top">Congratulations.  Outstanding photo.</td>', 'Congratulations.  Outstanding photo.', '2008-02-08 10:55:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470931, 638581, 11854, '<td valign="top">I also found the guy on the right, coming into the frame distracting. I love the focus on the girl though, and how her smile comes through with the chaos of the city all around her.</td>', 'I also found the guy on the right, coming into the frame distracting. I love the focus on the girl though, and how her smile comes through with the chaos of the city all around her.', '2008-02-08 10:55:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470934, 629050, 63398, '<td valign="top">Kelli, I like it ''cause of being a Pennsylvania boy and knowing about the Mummer''s Parade. That said, I think it got slammed because of there not being so much of a defined subject in spite of the reveler in center stage. It''s very busty, and honestly, he doesn''t stanmd out from the other celebrants, but they are glaringly different from their surroundings.<br/> <br/>But you still have a fun, cool shot for the memories!!!  I LOVE his/her costume!!! Nice job!</td>', 'Kelli, I like it ''cause of being a Pennsylvania boy and knowing about the Mummer''s Parade. That said, I think it got slammed because of there not being so much of a defined subject in spite of the reveler in center stage. It''s very busty, and honestly, he doesn''t stanmd out from the other celebrants, but they are glaringly different from their surroundings. But you still have a fun, cool shot for the memories!!!  I LOVE his/her costume!!! Nice job!', '2008-02-08 10:56:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470936, 640490, 30049, '<td valign="top">I like the lines that the edge of the mountain creates.  The color of the mountains against the blue sky also works well.<br/> <br/>The primary subject to me is the moon.  That''s the first thing that gets my attention.  The mountain hillsides are quite busy and there''s nothing to lock onto...so to the moon I go.  :)  Problem is, the moon seems oversharpened and gives it an almost artificial look, like it was cut &amp; pasted in from somewhere else.<br/> <br/>While some may say that the image is too compositionally centered, I think it adds some balance.  If the moon had been higher in the sky, then I may have considered cropping to remove some of the lower half of the photo.<br/> <br/>All JMO of course.  :-D</td>', 'I like the lines that the edge of the mountain creates.  The color of the mountains against the blue sky also works well. The primary subject to me is the moon.  That''s the first thing that gets my attention.  The mountain hillsides are quite busy and there''s nothing to lock onto...so to the moon I go.  :)  Problem is, the moon seems oversharpened and gives it an almost artificial look, like it was cut & pasted in from somewhere else. While some may say that the image is too compositionally centered, I think it adds some balance.  If the moon had been higher in the sky, then I may have considered cropping to remove some of the lower half of the photo. All JMO of course.  :-D', '2008-02-08 10:57:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470937, 640852, 42495, '<td valign="top">Congrats Neil - this is stunning and a great example of HDR done right.  How many shots did you bracket and what exposure?</td>', 'Congrats Neil - this is stunning and a great example of HDR done right.  How many shots did you bracket and what exposure?', '2008-02-08 10:57:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470938, 639576, 67697, '<td valign="top">Very nice in black and white.  I like the lone one in the foreground and the others in the background.  The arch of the bridge(?) in the background is a nice complement to the arched supports of the benches.</td>', 'Very nice in black and white.  I like the lone one in the foreground and the others in the background.  The arch of the bridge(?) in the background is a nice complement to the arched supports of the benches.', '2008-02-08 10:58:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470942, 640677, 67697, '<td valign="top">Too bad, I thought this would have scored higher.  I gave it a 7.  The first thing that caught my attention were those big, beautiful eyes!  Such a sweet face.  I''m sure this will make a great keepsake!</td>', 'Too bad, I thought this would have scored higher.  I gave it a 7.  The first thing that caught my attention were those big, beautiful eyes!  Such a sweet face.  I''m sure this will make a great keepsake!', '2008-02-08 11:00:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470945, 640703, 60495, '<td valign="top">I really liked this one, I gave it a 7 also. If I were to change anything it would be to get rid of the remaining detail in the white opening to take away a bit of distraction and since it is smaller than a parking lot it should be legal....lol</td>', 'I really liked this one, I gave it a 7 also. If I were to change anything it would be to get rid of the remaining detail in the white opening to take away a bit of distraction and since it is smaller than a parking lot it should be legal....lol', '2008-02-08 11:02:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470947, 638604, 67697, '<td valign="top">Very pretty!  I''m going to have to get out to the metroparks.  FYI - there''s a lot running around the Ottawa National Wildlife Refuge too.  I love the contrast of the browns against the white background.  It was very nice of them to stop and pose for you like this.  :)</td>', 'Very pretty!  I''m going to have to get out to the metroparks.  FYI - there''s a lot running around the Ottawa National Wildlife Refuge too.  I love the contrast of the browns against the white background.  It was very nice of them to stop and pose for you like this.  :)', '2008-02-08 11:03:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470951, 635468, 63398, '<td valign="top">LOL!!! I''m probably not the right person to evaluate this image....mine:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=640942" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/640942.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/640942.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/640942.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I love the composition, not so much the color/tone processing. I''d love to see this in a low or no-sat version. It should have done better IMO. It is a lovely, peaceful setting.</td>', 'LOL!!! I''m probably not the right person to evaluate this image....mine:  I love the composition, not so much the color/tone processing. I''d love to see this in a low or no-sat version. It should have done better IMO. It is a lovely, peaceful setting.', '2008-02-08 11:04:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470958, 636144, 67697, '<td valign="top">I''m kind of chuckling at the comments you got.  I guess since I live in a small town, I kind of like the busy-ness of the photo.  I like seeing the action of all the people moving about.  I love the clarity of the whole scene and the pop of color adds life to the buildings.  I gave this a 6 because I think I did not like the one tall building being cut off.  I''m not sure what others meant by perspective correction but it would be cool to see what the photo would look like if you had taken this from a portrait (instead of landscape) orienatation.</td>', 'I''m kind of chuckling at the comments you got.  I guess since I live in a small town, I kind of like the busy-ness of the photo.  I like seeing the action of all the people moving about.  I love the clarity of the whole scene and the pop of color adds life to the buildings.  I gave this a 6 because I think I did not like the one tall building being cut off.  I''m not sure what others meant by perspective correction but it would be cool to see what the photo would look like if you had taken this from a portrait (instead of landscape) orienatation.', '2008-02-08 11:08:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470964, 640819, 63398, '<td valign="top">I kind of agree about the tree seeming at odds somewhat, but I also see Kelli''s perspective about the tree crying, though I wouldn''t have seen that myself. I do like the B&amp;W conversion as it works well with the lighting. All in all not a bad image at all IMO. I''m always a sucker for ripples &amp; reflections.</td>', 'I kind of agree about the tree seeming at odds somewhat, but I also see Kelli''s perspective about the tree crying, though I wouldn''t have seen that myself. I do like the B&W conversion as it works well with the lighting. All in all not a bad image at all IMO. I''m always a sucker for ripples & reflections.', '2008-02-08 11:12:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470965, 640854, 30049, '<td valign="top">The first thing I catch when viewing this is the wingtips just touching the sand.  Then the presence of the reflection and it''s resulting odd circle.  Isolation of the subject, via high contrast, works very well.<br/> <br/>That''s my first impression.<br/> <br/>Then to get critical, after all this is DPC right?...I notice some other things, good and ok.  The birds shadow.  I missed it at first.  Adds another element of interest - that''s good.  :)  The birds feet outstretched behind in flight.  Didn''t catch that initially, but it adds in giving a sense of urgency and timing to the capture.  The sand, the water, the pelican, all worked to tell me this was taken at the shoreline...the washed out lapping water in the bg confirm that upon further review (doesn''t add nor take away).  Yes, the bird is a tad blurry in spots (mostly motion blur? on the leading wing) - would the image be stronger if the entire bird was spot on...yes, but it doesn''t entirely kill the photo because it''s not.<br/> <br/>All JMO of course.  Nice capture overall.</td>', 'The first thing I catch when viewing this is the wingtips just touching the sand.  Then the presence of the reflection and it''s resulting odd circle.  Isolation of the subject, via high contrast, works very well. That''s my first impression. Then to get critical, after all this is DPC right?...I notice some other things, good and ok.  The birds shadow.  I missed it at first.  Adds another element of interest - that''s good.  :)  The birds feet outstretched behind in flight.  Didn''t catch that initially, but it adds in giving a sense of urgency and timing to the capture.  The sand, the water, the pelican, all worked to tell me this was taken at the shoreline...the washed out lapping water in the bg confirm that upon further review (doesn''t add nor take away).  Yes, the bird is a tad blurry in spots (mostly motion blur? on the leading wing) - would the image be stronger if the entire bird was spot on...yes, but it doesn''t entirely kill the photo because it''s not. All JMO of course.  Nice capture overall.', '2008-02-08 11:12:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470966, 640872, 67697, '<td valign="top">lol I hardly think this is overdone.  methinks maybe someone has not been at DPC long enough.  I love the arched and flowing clouds and how it looks like they are going to move out of the frame.  Beautiful colors in the sun and sky.  I love the reflection as well.  Pretty scene!</td>', 'lol I hardly think this is overdone.  methinks maybe someone has not been at DPC long enough.  I love the arched and flowing clouds and how it looks like they are going to move out of the frame.  Beautiful colors in the sun and sky.  I love the reflection as well.  Pretty scene!', '2008-02-08 11:13:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470968, 639327, 63398, '<td valign="top">I have absolutely no idea whatsoever why this didn''t score better.<br/> <br/>The only thing I could possibly think of to do would maybe to have cropped it a little differently on the right to move him to the side of the image and possibly to lighten it to bring up his clothing.<br/> <br/>I like it!</td>', 'I have absolutely no idea whatsoever why this didn''t score better. The only thing I could possibly think of to do would maybe to have cropped it a little differently on the right to move him to the side of the image and possibly to lighten it to bring up his clothing. I like it!', '2008-02-08 11:14:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470972, 640854, 67697, '<td valign="top">lol you know you should have called this "doing pushups - birdie style".  That is what it looks like he is doing! It''s so cool how the wing-tips are just grazing the water and the feet are sticking up behind him.  What great timing for this catch!</td>', 'lol you know you should have called this "doing pushups - birdie style".  That is what it looks like he is doing! It''s so cool how the wing-tips are just grazing the water and the feet are sticking up behind him.  What great timing for this catch!', '2008-02-08 11:17:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470975, 639468, 39184, '<td valign="top">I agree with the previous two comments.  The main subject that I want to land upon is the distant city with the red glow, but the foreground buildings keep bringing my eyes back to them and that''s not the ''pretty'' part of the image.  The tallest building interrupts the nicest part of the image which extends to the left of that building.  So, to frame the center part of the shot with the tall building (or just part of it) framing the left side would improve this shot a lot.  Maybe if you could just hop over to the next roof in the center or to the one on the right (it''s closer) and compose the shot from there ;)<br/> <br/>BTW, good idea for a nighttime shot.  I think you have a great area to work with. <i>edit spelling</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 11:21:08.</i></td>', 'I agree with the previous two comments.  The main subject that I want to land upon is the distant city with the red glow, but the foreground buildings keep bringing my eyes back to them and that''s not the ''pretty'' part of the image.  The tallest building interrupts the nicest part of the image which extends to the left of that building.  So, to frame the center part of the shot with the tall building (or just part of it) framing the left side would improve this shot a lot.  Maybe if you could just hop over to the next roof in the center or to the one on the right (it''s closer) and compose the shot from there ;) BTW, good idea for a nighttime shot.  I think you have a great area to work with. edit spelling', '2008-02-08 11:20:24.000000', '2008-02-08 11:21:08.000000', 0),
(4470976, 638581, 30049, '<td valign="top">B/W was certainly the way to go with this and you have a nice tonal range overall.  The strong side lighting makes this photo work.  You couldn''t have pulled this off a couple hours later.  This lighting provides some detail in the shadows and nice highlighting.  Did you notice the camera ladies shadow is interrupted by the floor drain?  :-)<br/> <br/>The archway helps contain this in a natural frame; even the sign post in the background helps, in that it directs the viewer to the double-decker bus in the background.  That in itself identifies the place for most viewers, giving this some additional context.<br/> <br/>Busy, busy, busy...hustle &amp; bustle, with so many people milling about.  The foreground man moving into the image adds a sense of urgency.  Yet, the gal with the camera says this is some place special and time stands still for a few in the moment.<br/> <br/>Nicely seen and captured.  Good story telling!  :)<br/> <br/>ETA - I just noticed that this shot only had 2 comments during the challenge period.  Guess there was too much to take in during the short look each photo is given during the voting stage.<br/> <br/>I usually don''t read other comments prior to making mine.  Don''t like to be unduly influenced.  :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 11:23:57.</i></td>', 'B/W was certainly the way to go with this and you have a nice tonal range overall.  The strong side lighting makes this photo work.  You couldn''t have pulled this off a couple hours later.  This lighting provides some detail in the shadows and nice highlighting.  Did you notice the camera ladies shadow is interrupted by the floor drain?  :-) The archway helps contain this in a natural frame; even the sign post in the background helps, in that it directs the viewer to the double-decker bus in the background.  That in itself identifies the place for most viewers, giving this some additional context. Busy, busy, busy...hustle & bustle, with so many people milling about.  The foreground man moving into the image adds a sense of urgency.  Yet, the gal with the camera says this is some place special and time stands still for a few in the moment. Nicely seen and captured.  Good story telling!  :) ETA - I just noticed that this shot only had 2 comments during the challenge period.  Guess there was too much to take in during the short look each photo is given during the voting stage. I usually don''t read other comments prior to making mine.  Don''t like to be unduly influenced.  :)', '2008-02-08 11:21:14.000000', '2008-02-08 11:23:57.000000', 0),
(4470985, 640060, 71459, '<td valign="top">Thanks Everyone! :)</td>', 'Thanks Everyone! :)', '2008-02-08 11:26:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470987, 638823, 71608, '<td valign="top">I like how soft this feels, despite it being sharp where it''s meant to be... I just realised it''s an infrared, and I think it works well! Makes it feel high-key, without blowing anything out :)</td>', 'I like how soft this feels, despite it being sharp where it''s meant to be... I just realised it''s an infrared, and I think it works well! Makes it feel high-key, without blowing anything out :)', '2008-02-08 11:28:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470991, 640398, 26733, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!</td>', 'Beautiful!', '2008-02-08 11:30:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4470994, 640035, 30049, '<td valign="top">High contrast, cold (rhododendrons tell me that), busy, interesting...all first impressions.<br/> <br/>Love the title.  I''ve seen several places like this along the Shenandoahs here in Virginia.  Love to stop when I can as you never know what "treasures" you might find!<br/> <br/>You know what pulls me away in this photo?  The powerline in the bg.  It''s a thick white line that just jumps out no matter how much I try to avoid it.<br/> <br/>What was your primary subject?  The building, or the sign?  I ask because your choice of aperture puts the sign squarely in focus, and teases with the building (not OOF for just bg, not sharp enough for comfortable viewing).  Tough choice for sure.  Go deeper and you bring in more "things" like branches, etc...go shallower and people will say they want more.  Hmmm.  Maybe you did make the correct aperture selection after all.  :-D<br/> <br/>Now you''ve made me want to take a road trip!  He-he.</td>', 'High contrast, cold (rhododendrons tell me that), busy, interesting...all first impressions. Love the title.  I''ve seen several places like this along the Shenandoahs here in Virginia.  Love to stop when I can as you never know what "treasures" you might find! You know what pulls me away in this photo?  The powerline in the bg.  It''s a thick white line that just jumps out no matter how much I try to avoid it. What was your primary subject?  The building, or the sign?  I ask because your choice of aperture puts the sign squarely in focus, and teases with the building (not OOF for just bg, not sharp enough for comfortable viewing).  Tough choice for sure.  Go deeper and you bring in more "things" like branches, etc...go shallower and people will say they want more.  Hmmm.  Maybe you did make the correct aperture selection after all.  :-D Now you''ve made me want to take a road trip!  He-he.', '2008-02-08 11:32:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471006, 640035, 811, '<td valign="top">yea. that blasted powerline bothered me too.  i tried to get rid of it, and just couldn''t get it to pass muster. .  ..</td>', 'yea. that blasted powerline bothered me too.  i tried to get rid of it, and just couldn''t get it to pass muster. .  ..', '2008-02-08 11:36:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471010, 640974, 30049, '<td valign="top">What''s he looking at?  Why''s his tail wagging (love the hint of motion BTW)?  There''s a story here.  That''s the first thing I think of.  Then I want to know what he looks like but I''m bummed because as the viewer I''ll never know.<br/> <br/>I do like how the lines in the pavement/sidewalk radiate out like they are pointing to the main subject.  The diagonal that the dog is on adds tension (in a good way) to those.<br/> <br/>Could be a tad underexposed?  Overall, it''s "ok", but one that probably was moved along fairly quickly during voting.<br/> <br/>All JMO of course.  :-)</td>', 'What''s he looking at?  Why''s his tail wagging (love the hint of motion BTW)?  There''s a story here.  That''s the first thing I think of.  Then I want to know what he looks like but I''m bummed because as the viewer I''ll never know. I do like how the lines in the pavement/sidewalk radiate out like they are pointing to the main subject.  The diagonal that the dog is on adds tension (in a good way) to those. Could be a tad underexposed?  Overall, it''s "ok", but one that probably was moved along fairly quickly during voting. All JMO of course.  :-)', '2008-02-08 11:39:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471046, 629050, 7743, '<td valign="top">I think you''ve captured the quirkiness.  What I noticed looking at it is that the front row of marchers lines up perfectly with the character who ''stepped'' into your shot.  I think a closer crop emphasizing that aspect of the image would provide greater impact.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 12:03:30.</i></td>', 'I think you''ve captured the quirkiness.  What I noticed looking at it is that the front row of marchers lines up perfectly with the character who ''stepped'' into your shot.  I think a closer crop emphasizing that aspect of the image would provide greater impact.', '2008-02-08 11:54:49.000000', '2008-02-08 12:03:30.000000', 0),
(4471064, 632908, 83032, '<td valign="top">Julianne, this is a response from the forum you signed up for:  It has already been said in a few of the comments and I agree; shots of toys or figurines don''t do well here.  The photo does have great bokeh that picked up the greenish dusk.  On the down side of the dust is that it gathered in the eyes and makes me want to flince alittle because we can all relate to getting something in your eyes and how painful that is.  I''ve looked thru your portfollio and you take some wonderful shots but I can''t say this is one of them.  Don''t be too discouraged by my comments, it''s just how one viewer sees this.  Do keep shooting, you do some really nice work.  X</td>', 'Julianne, this is a response from the forum you signed up for:  It has already been said in a few of the comments and I agree; shots of toys or figurines don''t do well here.  The photo does have great bokeh that picked up the greenish dusk.  On the down side of the dust is that it gathered in the eyes and makes me want to flince alittle because we can all relate to getting something in your eyes and how painful that is.  I''ve looked thru your portfollio and you take some wonderful shots but I can''t say this is one of them.  Don''t be too discouraged by my comments, it''s just how one viewer sees this.  Do keep shooting, you do some really nice work.  X', '2008-02-08 12:01:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471081, 634908, 61651, '<td valign="top">I like how you framed this, the position of the goat on the diagonal gives the eye some direction, and gives it a bit of energy.  The overall light does seem a bit dull, though - some levels adjustment might brighten things up a bit?</td>', 'I like how you framed this, the position of the goat on the diagonal gives the eye some direction, and gives it a bit of energy.  The overall light does seem a bit dull, though - some levels adjustment might brighten things up a bit?', '2008-02-08 12:08:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471091, 640401, 61651, '<td valign="top">The pose and framing is attractive - nice lock-you-in gaze - but the blown hair on the right is noticeable enough to be distracting, to me.  I don''t know how you lit it or whether you had control over the lighting, but the light on that side might have been better off minimized somewhat.</td>', 'The pose and framing is attractive - nice lock-you-in gaze - but the blown hair on the right is noticeable enough to be distracting, to me.  I don''t know how you lit it or whether you had control over the lighting, but the light on that side might have been better off minimized somewhat.', '2008-02-08 12:13:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471097, 638490, 34956, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all comments. orvaratli you are right I should have used that one, this is not the same picture I shot 4 pic of the Hut that night and the ljosmyndakeppni.is entry was best of them but I was not sure if I could use it here because it had already won there and on steves-digicam.com photo of the day to.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 15:30:00.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all comments. orvaratli you are right I should have used that one, this is not the same picture I shot 4 pic of the Hut that night and the ljosmyndakeppni.is entry was best of them but I was not sure if I could use it here because it had already won there and on steves-digicam.com photo of the day to.', '2008-02-08 12:16:36.000000', '2008-02-08 15:30:00.000000', 0),
(4471104, 640231, 61651, '<td valign="top">Yeah, at first I thought that rose what attached to her hair, too!  I like the rich colors - suits the subject matter.  There may have been a cringe factor with the voting on this photo - I remember when I first came across this picture my first thought was "ouch"!  :)</td>', 'Yeah, at first I thought that rose what attached to her hair, too!  I like the rich colors - suits the subject matter.  There may have been a cringe factor with the voting on this photo - I remember when I first came across this picture my first thought was "ouch"!  :)', '2008-02-08 12:18:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471113, 638137, 66952, '<td valign="top">A well deserved blue. I love the lines leading to the mountain, and the detail on both the snow and mountain.</td>', 'A well deserved blue. I love the lines leading to the mountain, and the detail on both the snow and mountain.', '2008-02-08 12:22:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471116, 640430, 61651, '<td valign="top">Hey, this was a 9 for me - I liked the offhand quirkiness, and how the reflection of the street in the screen makes it look as if that is what the tv is broadcasting.  The muted colors suit the vintage feel.</td>', 'Hey, this was a 9 for me - I liked the offhand quirkiness, and how the reflection of the street in the screen makes it look as if that is what the tv is broadcasting.  The muted colors suit the vintage feel.', '2008-02-08 12:24:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471123, 640756, 61651, '<td valign="top">Well, you already know how I feel about this one, Rob - glad that you entered somewhere.  I do like this minimalist look.  It''s about feeling, not about needing to see every detail.</td>', 'Well, you already know how I feel about this one, Rob - glad that you entered somewhere.  I do like this minimalist look.  It''s about feeling, not about needing to see every detail.', '2008-02-08 12:25:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471126, 640231, 83032, '<td valign="top">Ingrid,<br/> <br/>I agree with Kelli''s comment: tatooing on women turn a lot of people off and I wouldn''t doubt that it has contributed to your low score as much as anything.  Also, in your PP some of the green has shown up in her hair and her skin tones. The left arm has been blown out and maybe you could have saved some of it using adjustment layers and playing with the contrast.  The composition looks good and the expression on her face relays just a hint of pain (and I''m not sure that is good or not).  Looking at other shots in your portfollio, I say this is not one of your best but that you do have an eye and have the potential of being a really good photographer.  Best of Luck.  X</td>', 'Ingrid, I agree with Kelli''s comment: tatooing on women turn a lot of people off and I wouldn''t doubt that it has contributed to your low score as much as anything.  Also, in your PP some of the green has shown up in her hair and her skin tones. The left arm has been blown out and maybe you could have saved some of it using adjustment layers and playing with the contrast.  The composition looks good and the expression on her face relays just a hint of pain (and I''m not sure that is good or not).  Looking at other shots in your portfollio, I say this is not one of your best but that you do have an eye and have the potential of being a really good photographer.  Best of Luck.  X', '2008-02-08 12:26:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471133, 640943, 61651, '<td valign="top">Good pose you captured there, with the head in profile and one foot lifted - really gives the viewer the sense of action, even though it can''t ever be anything but a static shot.  I put a piece of paper at the top to get a sense of what it would look like cropped, as another commenter suggested you might do - it is possible with the crop that the goose may have been more visually isolated, without the contrasting background drawing the eye away.</td>', 'Good pose you captured there, with the head in profile and one foot lifted - really gives the viewer the sense of action, even though it can''t ever be anything but a static shot.  I put a piece of paper at the top to get a sense of what it would look like cropped, as another commenter suggested you might do - it is possible with the crop that the goose may have been more visually isolated, without the contrasting background drawing the eye away.', '2008-02-08 12:29:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471134, 632070, 66952, '<td valign="top">Alain, I did the same thing. I had a portrait entered in the FS, then backed it out and entered a second shot of the same hummingbird. I a lot of ways, I like this one better than your other eagle. Both are great shots, and I like being able to see into the mouth of the other one, but the composition and exposure control on this one are better. <br/> <br/>Both excellent, though.</td>', 'Alain, I did the same thing. I had a portrait entered in the FS, then backed it out and entered a second shot of the same hummingbird. I a lot of ways, I like this one better than your other eagle. Both are great shots, and I like being able to see into the mouth of the other one, but the composition and exposure control on this one are better.  Both excellent, though.', '2008-02-08 12:29:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471138, 640401, 54843, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments so far.  I am beginning to understand why this image did not do as well as I was expecting.  The blown highlight was actually intentional...although not necessarily for this specific image.  I had set up a strobe behind Sarah to highlight the hair, which was being blown around by a fan.  This gives a VERY cool effect.  However, the effect is mostly lost when I convert to B&amp;W or crop heavily.  This image did both, so the effect was lost and actuallly became a distraction.  <br/> <br/>I plan on making another version with the entire right side cropped out to get rid of the blown highlight.  It will be a different compostion, but the eyes should still make for a decent image.<br/> <br/>Any other comments?<br/> <br/>PS - I will be posting some more images from this shoot for everyone to look at and comment on.  Hopefully tonight...<br/> <br/>PPS - see the effect in another image of mine --<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=312133" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/54843/120/312133.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/54843/120/312133.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/54843/120/312133.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 12:40:44.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments so far.  I am beginning to understand why this image did not do as well as I was expecting.  The blown highlight was actually intentional...although not necessarily for this specific image.  I had set up a strobe behind Sarah to highlight the hair, which was being blown around by a fan.  This gives a VERY cool effect.  However, the effect is mostly lost when I convert to B&W or crop heavily.  This image did both, so the effect was lost and actuallly became a distraction.   I plan on making another version with the entire right side cropped out to get rid of the blown highlight.  It will be a different compostion, but the eyes should still make for a decent image. Any other comments? PS - I will be posting some more images from this shoot for everyone to look at and comment on.  Hopefully tonight... PPS - see the effect in another image of mine -- ', '2008-02-08 12:31:13.000000', '2008-02-08 12:40:44.000000', 0),
(4471139, 640534, 61651, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a lovely concept - the sundial.  Good strong color contrasts, of the "moody" feel, which suits the battered-looking landscape.  Your score is darn respectable!</td>', 'I thought this was a lovely concept - the sundial.  Good strong color contrasts, of the "moody" feel, which suits the battered-looking landscape.  Your score is darn respectable!', '2008-02-08 12:31:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471140, 631825, 80912, '<td valign="top">I think it was the dead center horizontal composition that made me score this low. Also the trees, buildings and fence in the background distracted me - their color and texture was more interesting. (I gave it a 5)</td>', 'I think it was the dead center horizontal composition that made me score this low. Also the trees, buildings and fence in the background distracted me - their color and texture was more interesting. (I gave it a 5)', '2008-02-08 12:31:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471145, 630611, 16912, '<td valign="top">What can I say other than Congratulations MAK! Wasn''t the landslide victory for you that I''m sure many where expecting and you were right, I needed a PB to get you.<br/> <br/>No wonder I never saw this as yours, was looking for an HDRI landscape lol. You certainly captured the moment here m8 - congrats (honestly!)<br/> <br/></td>', 'What can I say other than Congratulations MAK! Wasn''t the landslide victory for you that I''m sure many where expecting and you were right, I needed a PB to get you. No wonder I never saw this as yours, was looking for an HDRI landscape lol. You certainly captured the moment here m8 - congrats (honestly!) ', '2008-02-08 12:32:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471146, 638823, 83032, '<td valign="top">Karen,<br/> <br/>You signed up in the forum and I am in your group, however I don''t feel I can do the piece justice commenting on it.  I''m not an infrared fan and your shot is just not doing anything for me.  I''ve looked over it for quite some time and I don''t have anything to say that could help you.  I have looked thru you portfollio and you have some really wonderful work there.  You have a really good eye and I think you make a good photographer.  Sorry I can''t help with this specific shot....keep shooting and good luck.  X</td>', 'Karen, You signed up in the forum and I am in your group, however I don''t feel I can do the piece justice commenting on it.  I''m not an infrared fan and your shot is just not doing anything for me.  I''ve looked over it for quite some time and I don''t have anything to say that could help you.  I have looked thru you portfollio and you have some really wonderful work there.  You have a really good eye and I think you make a good photographer.  Sorry I can''t help with this specific shot....keep shooting and good luck.  X', '2008-02-08 12:33:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471152, 634256, 80912, '<td valign="top">I really liked this, but only gave it a 7. The composition was beautiful, and I loved the jewel-like quality, but I wanted to see more detail.</td>', 'I really liked this, but only gave it a 7. The composition was beautiful, and I loved the jewel-like quality, but I wanted to see more detail.', '2008-02-08 12:35:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471153, 640398, 66952, '<td valign="top">Yours and DrAchoo''s were the only 10''s I gave in this challenge. Beautiful location, excellent processing, what''s not to love? Congrats on the red.</td>', 'Yours and DrAchoo''s were the only 10''s I gave in this challenge. Beautiful location, excellent processing, what''s not to love? Congrats on the red.', '2008-02-08 12:36:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471154, 638112, 61651, '<td valign="top">Usually zoom effects like this are really noticeable, this one is subtle - I admit I missed it when I first saw it.    I gave this a 6, which for me means average-but-with-great-promise - if I had gone back to review my votes like I meant to, this one may have gotten a bump.  This is really quite a lovely shot!</td>', 'Usually zoom effects like this are really noticeable, this one is subtle - I admit I missed it when I first saw it.    I gave this a 6, which for me means average-but-with-great-promise - if I had gone back to review my votes like I meant to, this one may have gotten a bump.  This is really quite a lovely shot!', '2008-02-08 12:36:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471157, 637941, 66952, '<td valign="top">This is one of the two 10''s I gave for this challenge (Larus was the other). I love the texture on the water, and the greens. Great stuff.</td>', 'This is one of the two 10''s I gave for this challenge (Larus was the other). I love the texture on the water, and the greens. Great stuff.', '2008-02-08 12:39:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471158, 639497, 80912, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this one, and I''m not sure what I would give it. My overall impression is of something missing - more detail, more sky, more of something that was cropped out? I''m not sure what.</td>', 'I didn''t vote on this one, and I''m not sure what I would give it. My overall impression is of something missing - more detail, more sky, more of something that was cropped out? I''m not sure what.', '2008-02-08 12:39:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471161, 640401, 83032, '<td valign="top">Josh,<br/> <br/>I like this shot very much and feel it should have scored a higher score.  You''ve got the info about the blow out....would have been nice to see the color version.  When you do another version you might try and move her to the right, alittle more towards the center.  You''ve done a really good job controling the lighting and keeping her face soft....all in all, I think it''s a great shot.  Keep up the good work.  She photographs well....would like to see more of her in the future.  Best of luck.  X</td>', 'Josh, I like this shot very much and feel it should have scored a higher score.  You''ve got the info about the blow out....would have been nice to see the color version.  When you do another version you might try and move her to the right, alittle more towards the center.  You''ve done a really good job controling the lighting and keeping her face soft....all in all, I think it''s a great shot.  Keep up the good work.  She photographs well....would like to see more of her in the future.  Best of luck.  X', '2008-02-08 12:41:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471163, 638632, 19708, '<td valign="top">Wonderful image and can think of nothing else that could make it any better, other than a wide mat and a frame, and of course getting it on a wall to be enjoyed in her home, for decades to come. This is truly what a camera is for - preserving the memories of our lives, as they can never be replicated.<br/> <br/><u>Edited to add:</u> <br/>The more I looked at this, the more it hit me it the white point was a bit off and could use with a levels adjustment to brighten it up a touch and give to look of added contrast without the harsh effects of contrast adjustment only. Here is what I came up with:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=644012" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/19708/120/644012.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/19708/120/644012.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/19708/120/644012.jpg"/></a> and the one step adjustment: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=644013" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/19708/120/644013.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/19708/120/644013.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/19708/120/644013.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>(<i>my monitor is calibrated with a Spyder3 btw</i>)<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 13:36:06.</i></td>', 'Wonderful image and can think of nothing else that could make it any better, other than a wide mat and a frame, and of course getting it on a wall to be enjoyed in her home, for decades to come. This is truly what a camera is for - preserving the memories of our lives, as they can never be replicated. Edited to add: The more I looked at this, the more it hit me it the white point was a bit off and could use with a levels adjustment to brighten it up a touch and give to look of added contrast without the harsh effects of contrast adjustment only. Here is what I came up with:  and the one step adjustment:   (my monitor is calibrated with a Spyder3 btw)', '2008-02-08 12:42:52.000000', '2008-02-08 13:36:06.000000', 0),
(4471165, 640872, 80912, '<td valign="top">I liked this, but only gave it a 6. The big black smudge of cloud on the right was what was too much for me. It conflicted too much w/ the colors and mood of the rest of the shot.</td>', 'I liked this, but only gave it a 6. The big black smudge of cloud on the right was what was too much for me. It conflicted too much w/ the colors and mood of the rest of the shot.', '2008-02-08 12:44:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471166, 640942, 61651, '<td valign="top">A great landscape shot with great lighting - all good.  To make it stand out from the pack though, that''s another thing entirely, especially in one of these huge free studies.  From my perspective, the composition here is good, but it is also, to be fair, predictable.  I like another commenter''s suggestion you get down lower, try a different perspective.  This really is a good location - maybe also try a similar shot with a wider angle, so you can get closer and not lose the breadth of view as you have here?</td>', 'A great landscape shot with great lighting - all good.  To make it stand out from the pack though, that''s another thing entirely, especially in one of these huge free studies.  From my perspective, the composition here is good, but it is also, to be fair, predictable.  I like another commenter''s suggestion you get down lower, try a different perspective.  This really is a good location - maybe also try a similar shot with a wider angle, so you can get closer and not lose the breadth of view as you have here?', '2008-02-08 12:45:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471172, 638552, 80912, '<td valign="top">I agree w/ ingridblue - the other 2 clumps of berries are what throw this off for me. They don''t blend into the background, so they pull focus,a nd yet they are out of focus. The bokeh of the background is amazing, though.</td>', 'I agree w/ ingridblue - the other 2 clumps of berries are what throw this off for me. They don''t blend into the background, so they pull focus,a nd yet they are out of focus. The bokeh of the background is amazing, though.', '2008-02-08 12:48:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471174, 635468, 61651, '<td valign="top">I like your dark version better, to be honest.  This one has it''s charms - the nice pastel colors for one - but I find myself wishing there were more contrast and detail to be seen in the very center of the shot, all the crowded together branches and shrub.</td>', 'I like your dark version better, to be honest.  This one has it''s charms - the nice pastel colors for one - but I find myself wishing there were more contrast and detail to be seen in the very center of the shot, all the crowded together branches and shrub.', '2008-02-08 12:50:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471182, 639327, 61651, '<td valign="top">I like how you caught the position of his feet - makes it looks like he''s about to do a little dance.  I find myself wishing he was a bit more isolated, without, particularly, that girl on the left coming out of his arm.</td>', 'I like how you caught the position of his feet - makes it looks like he''s about to do a little dance.  I find myself wishing he was a bit more isolated, without, particularly, that girl on the left coming out of his arm.', '2008-02-08 12:54:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471184, 629050, 61651, '<td valign="top">So, did they play "Monster Mash"? :)  I like how you caught him leaning back into that classic Mummer''s strut.</td>', 'So, did they play "Monster Mash"? :)  I like how you caught him leaning back into that classic Mummer''s strut.', '2008-02-08 12:57:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471193, 634256, 61651, '<td valign="top">Wonderful clarity to this, and I like how the branch spreads out much like how snow crystals do.</td>', 'Wonderful clarity to this, and I like how the branch spreads out much like how snow crystals do.', '2008-02-08 13:01:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471194, 638581, 80912, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8 (same score I gave the blue ribboner). I love the framing, and the light outlining several people (especially camera-girl). I think the blurred man in front helps add a sense of motion - this crowd is moving not just standing waiting for something (although a few are taking a rest, lol).<br/> <br/>And there is a wide range of several things - <br/> <br/>Light - from full sun in the background to partially lit/backlit to full shade (and yet it all clear and defined), <br/> <br/>Motion - from the moving crowd to the breifly stopped camera girl to the more stationary sitters, and<br/> <br/>Mood - blurry guy seems in a hurry or distracted, the woman and baby are just trying to get through the day, and camera girl is happy and exctied to be visiting the city.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I gave this an 8 (same score I gave the blue ribboner). I love the framing, and the light outlining several people (especially camera-girl). I think the blurred man in front helps add a sense of motion - this crowd is moving not just standing waiting for something (although a few are taking a rest, lol). And there is a wide range of several things -  Light - from full sun in the background to partially lit/backlit to full shade (and yet it all clear and defined),  Motion - from the moving crowd to the breifly stopped camera girl to the more stationary sitters, and Mood - blurry guy seems in a hurry or distracted, the woman and baby are just trying to get through the day, and camera girl is happy and exctied to be visiting the city. ', '2008-02-08 13:02:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471198, 640430, 80912, '<td valign="top">I thought this was beautifully surreal. I might have scored it higher if I had seen the reflection in the TV better - I see it now and love it.<br/> <br/>I only gave it a 6 though because of the color. It seems to have a greenish cast, and yet the green of the grass is faded. It''s like you couldn''t decide if you wanted it in color or B&amp;W and split the difference. I think I''d have liked it better either B&amp;W or w/ stronger colors (maybe even surreal colors).</td>', 'I thought this was beautifully surreal. I might have scored it higher if I had seen the reflection in the TV better - I see it now and love it. I only gave it a 6 though because of the color. It seems to have a greenish cast, and yet the green of the grass is faded. It''s like you couldn''t decide if you wanted it in color or B&W and split the difference. I think I''d have liked it better either B&W or w/ stronger colors (maybe even surreal colors).', '2008-02-08 13:08:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471199, 638548, 73980, '<td valign="top">freaking well done!</td>', 'freaking well done!', '2008-02-08 13:09:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471211, 637415, 73980, '<td valign="top">Very well done, congratulations!  Very dramatic</td>', 'Very well done, congratulations!  Very dramatic', '2008-02-08 13:14:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471216, 629050, 80912, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6. I like the central figure (and how he''s perfectly in line w/ the first row - I thought he was supposed to be part of that row when I voted!)<br/> <br/>I sort of like the feeling of motion - but fell the need for more clarity somewhere. Either have the marchers in focus (I''d really like to see more detail in them, although maybe that wouldn''t score well either), or have the buildings in focus to contrast w/ the blur of the moving marchers.<br/> <br/>Even as is, I don''t think it deserved such a low score.</td>', 'I gave this a 6. I like the central figure (and how he''s perfectly in line w/ the first row - I thought he was supposed to be part of that row when I voted!) I sort of like the feeling of motion - but fell the need for more clarity somewhere. Either have the marchers in focus (I''d really like to see more detail in them, although maybe that wouldn''t score well either), or have the buildings in focus to contrast w/ the blur of the moving marchers. Even as is, I don''t think it deserved such a low score.', '2008-02-08 13:17:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471226, 633017, 73980, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure what kind of lens you have, not familiar with it but the fact you are using a Rebel...  phew.<br/> <br/>Awesome shot, congratulations!</td>', 'I''m not sure what kind of lens you have, not familiar with it but the fact you are using a Rebel...  phew. Awesome shot, congratulations!', '2008-02-08 13:21:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471228, 638552, 83080, '<td valign="top">First, I''m a beginner, so take this with a grain of salt...<br/>I do like the shot overall.  The downside for me is that the bokeh feels distracting.   perhaps the bokeh is too well defined on the outer edges, so a little softer, centered bokeh may have felt warmer.  Also, I wonder what this shot would have looked like with just a little more DOF, allowing the sharpness to soften as you travel down the foreground branch.  The repeating curves are indeed really pleasing and the placement of the main subject is perfect.<br/> <br/>You have some great shots on your profile page and I hope to reach that level one day myself.  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=642559" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">They Went That-A-Way made me laugh</a>.</td>', 'First, I''m a beginner, so take this with a grain of salt...I do like the shot overall.  The downside for me is that the bokeh feels distracting.   perhaps the bokeh is too well defined on the outer edges, so a little softer, centered bokeh may have felt warmer.  Also, I wonder what this shot would have looked like with just a little more DOF, allowing the sharpness to soften as you travel down the foreground branch.  The repeating curves are indeed really pleasing and the placement of the main subject is perfect. You have some great shots on your profile page and I hope to reach that level one day myself.  They Went That-A-Way made me laugh.', '2008-02-08 13:21:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471233, 640651, 63244, '<td valign="top">There is really not much to nit on this shot IMO. I might have tried to play a little with shadow/highlights and get a touch more detail in the wood behind the gazeebo top (guessing that is what it is). It looks a touch flat due to the lighting in the shade This is such a great abstract shot, but I''m finding that abstract is not for the mainstream here, thus doesn''t score well in Free Study challenges. (Personlly, I like them very much!)  If someone were to get totally picky about this, the shot is every so slightly (minutely) not centered.  I think the shot is fun!!</td>', 'There is really not much to nit on this shot IMO. I might have tried to play a little with shadow/highlights and get a touch more detail in the wood behind the gazeebo top (guessing that is what it is). It looks a touch flat due to the lighting in the shade This is such a great abstract shot, but I''m finding that abstract is not for the mainstream here, thus doesn''t score well in Free Study challenges. (Personlly, I like them very much!)  If someone were to get totally picky about this, the shot is every so slightly (minutely) not centered.  I think the shot is fun!!', '2008-02-08 13:23:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471239, 640231, 64670, '<td valign="top">Oh MY - you tapped into a secret desire of mine - I have ALWAYS wanted to photograph someone (or many people being tattooed).<br/> <br/>I don''t have any myself, but the ''act'' of being tattooed really interests me.<br/> <br/>I think your candid is lovely - why the masses didn''t like it?<br/> <br/>Firstly I don''t think candids do well in free studys as a rule.<br/> <br/>Secondly, although I like the grainy &amp; less crisp look, for a free study it would have lost points.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oh MY - you tapped into a secret desire of mine - I have ALWAYS wanted to photograph someone (or many people being tattooed). I don''t have any myself, but the ''act'' of being tattooed really interests me. I think your candid is lovely - why the masses didn''t like it? Firstly I don''t think candids do well in free studys as a rule. Secondly, although I like the grainy & less crisp look, for a free study it would have lost points. ', '2008-02-08 13:25:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471241, 632039, 56109, '<td valign="top">I actually really like the lighthouse. I''m glad you kept it because IMO it gives the picture another element and detail.</td>', 'I actually really like the lighthouse. I''m glad you kept it because IMO it gives the picture another element and detail.', '2008-02-08 13:25:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471249, 640942, 80912, '<td valign="top">I scored this a 6. I definitely saw (and appreciated) the quiet beauty. OTOH, there was something about the processing (in the building and the tree in front of it) that seems harsh/over processed. Maybe too much contrast? I''m not good enough myself to pin it down, but it conflicted w/ the mood and pulled the score down for me.</td>', 'I scored this a 6. I definitely saw (and appreciated) the quiet beauty. OTOH, there was something about the processing (in the building and the tree in front of it) that seems harsh/over processed. Maybe too much contrast? I''m not good enough myself to pin it down, but it conflicted w/ the mood and pulled the score down for me.', '2008-02-08 13:28:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471254, 633017, 60698, '<td valign="top">Wow! This one stopped me short in my tracks. I had to stop by your portfolio and tour the universe! Your work is awesome! :)</td>', 'Wow! This one stopped me short in my tracks. I had to stop by your portfolio and tour the universe! Your work is awesome! :)', '2008-02-08 13:30:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471255, 638552, 63244, '<td valign="top">For the record, I love this shot.  This is the stuff i really enjoy looking at.  Your colors are very good.  I like the DOF, but think this may have fared a bit better had you gone a little deeper.  The berries are sharp, but the back of the cluster and even the branch attached to them starts to get OOF very quickly.  You have oof branch on both sides of the photo. The bokeh is great on this shot.  My only thought (and what do I know...) would be to make it a little different and rotate the shot CCW 90º to make it <i>very</i> different. Then you would commant the look of the viewer a bit more. By including the OOF berries it does show depth. Overall...I think it''s a very nice shot of a simple subject.</td>', 'For the record, I love this shot.  This is the stuff i really enjoy looking at.  Your colors are very good.  I like the DOF, but think this may have fared a bit better had you gone a little deeper.  The berries are sharp, but the back of the cluster and even the branch attached to them starts to get OOF very quickly.  You have oof branch on both sides of the photo. The bokeh is great on this shot.  My only thought (and what do I know...) would be to make it a little different and rotate the shot CCW 90º to make it very different. Then you would commant the look of the viewer a bit more. By including the OOF berries it does show depth. Overall...I think it''s a very nice shot of a simple subject.', '2008-02-08 13:30:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471262, 639497, 63244, '<td valign="top">I like the subject matter in this shot.  Because it is Advanced Editing, you might have wanted to try and pull a little more detail out of the sky.  On that note, it is a bit hard to determine whether you are making the sky the subject or the mountains. IMO, I might have tried cropping more of the sky out to make those beautiful mountains more of the subject. When it''s so close to center (not on a third), it gives equal weight to the sky and land, so you really have to have something dynamic in each to pull it off.  The focus and detail is very good.  perhaps a run at shadows and highlights might give it just a little extra "sparkle".  It''s a very pretty shot. (I am by far not an expert, nor do I play one on TV, so take all of this w/a bit of scepticism. :~}  )</td>', 'I like the subject matter in this shot.  Because it is Advanced Editing, you might have wanted to try and pull a little more detail out of the sky.  On that note, it is a bit hard to determine whether you are making the sky the subject or the mountains. IMO, I might have tried cropping more of the sky out to make those beautiful mountains more of the subject. When it''s so close to center (not on a third), it gives equal weight to the sky and land, so you really have to have something dynamic in each to pull it off.  The focus and detail is very good.  perhaps a run at shadows and highlights might give it just a little extra "sparkle".  It''s a very pretty shot. (I am by far not an expert, nor do I play one on TV, so take all of this w/a bit of scepticism. :~}  )', '2008-02-08 13:35:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471282, 634256, 63244, '<td valign="top">This has such potential.  I really, really like the composition and the whole concept.  Brilliant that you used the flash to bump the glisten.  The colors seem very accurate.  I wish the DOF was a touch deeper to encompass more of the branches.  i think you would still have great background bokeh, but you wouldn''t feel the need to "see more of the subject".  It looks a touch flat. maybe a bit more contrast or shadow/highlight to bring out a little more detail?? (What do I know.)  The frame is not adding to the photograph, IMO. :) Overall, I really like this shot. It''s sad that the "non''mainstream" shots don''t do better here.</td>', 'This has such potential.  I really, really like the composition and the whole concept.  Brilliant that you used the flash to bump the glisten.  The colors seem very accurate.  I wish the DOF was a touch deeper to encompass more of the branches.  i think you would still have great background bokeh, but you wouldn''t feel the need to "see more of the subject".  It looks a touch flat. maybe a bit more contrast or shadow/highlight to bring out a little more detail?? (What do I know.)  The frame is not adding to the photograph, IMO. :) Overall, I really like this shot. It''s sad that the "non''mainstream" shots don''t do better here.', '2008-02-08 13:45:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471299, 631825, 63244, '<td valign="top">Ok...I like the subject matter here.  You would have done much better shooting at a different time of day (early morning or late afternoon/evening) to get much better lighting.  The light here is a little harsh to me.  A much shorter DOF would have given more weight to the cars and given you a more diffused background and foreground.  A different perspective would have really helped on this one. (There is the issue of the big "hump" in the way from where this was shot.)  Had you been able to pull the clump of weeds away and gotten lower, this would have been much more interesting. Because the colors are not really dynamic, there needs to be something else to draw the viewer in, and unfortunately, there is a lot going on in this shot. :) (I''m no expert!)</td>', 'Ok...I like the subject matter here.  You would have done much better shooting at a different time of day (early morning or late afternoon/evening) to get much better lighting.  The light here is a little harsh to me.  A much shorter DOF would have given more weight to the cars and given you a more diffused background and foreground.  A different perspective would have really helped on this one. (There is the issue of the big "hump" in the way from where this was shot.)  Had you been able to pull the clump of weeds away and gotten lower, this would have been much more interesting. Because the colors are not really dynamic, there needs to be something else to draw the viewer in, and unfortunately, there is a lot going on in this shot. :) (I''m no expert!)', '2008-02-08 13:52:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471313, 640869, 82099, '<td valign="top">You definitely did the right thing in going with what you thought would connect with more people.  This is a great capture. Poor fish. Oh well, circle of life.</td>', 'You definitely did the right thing in going with what you thought would connect with more people.  This is a great capture. Poor fish. Oh well, circle of life.', '2008-02-08 13:58:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471316, 640596, 82099, '<td valign="top">Another excellent hummingbird shot by Ann!!Congrats!!</td>', 'Another excellent hummingbird shot by Ann!!Congrats!!', '2008-02-08 14:00:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471324, 640872, 83313, '<td valign="top">Looks pretty good. It''s got the great colors and swoopy clouds that always seem to do so well here. My thinking is that sunsets are so easy to obtain impressive shots from that people here don''t rate them as high anymore unless they stand out in some special way.<br/> <br/>I don''t think the horizon is too centered. However, if a little more had been cropped from the bottom, that might draw the eye to those awesome clouds a little more. I happen to like the black cloud. I think it adds a little more interest but being dark, it does not draw excessive attention away form the sunset.<br/> <br/>The horizon line seems curved downward in the middle slightly. Not much, but it''s obvious and a little unnatural looking. If it were curved upward in the middle that would look ok, because it''s what you expect from a wideangle lens.<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote on this one, but I would have probably given it a 6 or maybe a 7.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 14:06:38.</i></td>', 'Looks pretty good. It''s got the great colors and swoopy clouds that always seem to do so well here. My thinking is that sunsets are so easy to obtain impressive shots from that people here don''t rate them as high anymore unless they stand out in some special way. I don''t think the horizon is too centered. However, if a little more had been cropped from the bottom, that might draw the eye to those awesome clouds a little more. I happen to like the black cloud. I think it adds a little more interest but being dark, it does not draw excessive attention away form the sunset. The horizon line seems curved downward in the middle slightly. Not much, but it''s obvious and a little unnatural looking. If it were curved upward in the middle that would look ok, because it''s what you expect from a wideangle lens. I didn''t vote on this one, but I would have probably given it a 6 or maybe a 7.', '2008-02-08 14:05:48.000000', '2008-02-08 14:06:38.000000', 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4471334, 640059, 61651, '<td valign="top">Technically very good - nicely timed long exposure.  Maybe not colorful enough to suit the average voter?</td>', 'Technically very good - nicely timed long exposure.  Maybe not colorful enough to suit the average voter?', '2008-02-08 14:10:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471335, 637396, 61651, '<td valign="top">Very cool capture, unusual angle of the jelly fish adds interest, and the illusion that it is floating in outer space rather than in water makes for nice double take!</td>', 'Very cool capture, unusual angle of the jelly fish adds interest, and the illusion that it is floating in outer space rather than in water makes for nice double take!', '2008-02-08 14:12:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471338, 633148, 61651, '<td valign="top">This has a nice humor to it, and the overall coloring says "The Southwest" very well.  Very sad story about the town.</td>', 'This has a nice humor to it, and the overall coloring says "The Southwest" very well.  Very sad story about the town.', '2008-02-08 14:14:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471341, 640693, 61651, '<td valign="top">Pretty respectable score!  The direct framing complements the simplicity of the shot.  Very nice!</td>', 'Pretty respectable score!  The direct framing complements the simplicity of the shot.  Very nice!', '2008-02-08 14:15:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471343, 640869, 20608, '<td valign="top">Loverly shot, not much grain at this res and your shutter finger hit it perfectly. Congrats on your HM, yo kept this quiet''ish. 2 7''s in a row</td>', 'Loverly shot, not much grain at this res and your shutter finger hit it perfectly. Congrats on your HM, yo kept this quiet''ish. 2 7''s in a row', '2008-02-08 14:16:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471346, 640430, 16488, '<td valign="top">How beautifully seen!<br/>(I stumbled upon this in the "I love my shot" thread. I''m not in the thread nor was involved with the FS but feel compelled to share.)<br/> <br/>On seeing this I have an immediate sense of story. This retro-toned image with a period chair and tv combination strikes a chord. With the reflection of the living world in the tv screen the tv seems to replace the former occupant of the chair. It''s curbside--discarded. As if some old relative has passed away and their favorite chair and old tv are no longer wanted...a sore reminder of what is past or what has passed. The house is dated with its aluminum windows and siding. Even the gate post holds cobwebs. Everything is kept and clean but not kept up. How surreal this sunny day story. How solemn the doorway to the house.<br/> <br/>I love the choices you''ve made from composition to color. So glad I stumbled across this! Adding to my favorites. Thank you.</td>', 'How beautifully seen!(I stumbled upon this in the "I love my shot" thread. I''m not in the thread nor was involved with the FS but feel compelled to share.) On seeing this I have an immediate sense of story. This retro-toned image with a period chair and tv combination strikes a chord. With the reflection of the living world in the tv screen the tv seems to replace the former occupant of the chair. It''s curbside--discarded. As if some old relative has passed away and their favorite chair and old tv are no longer wanted...a sore reminder of what is past or what has passed. The house is dated with its aluminum windows and siding. Even the gate post holds cobwebs. Everything is kept and clean but not kept up. How surreal this sunny day story. How solemn the doorway to the house. I love the choices you''ve made from composition to color. So glad I stumbled across this! Adding to my favorites. Thank you.', '2008-02-08 14:18:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471347, 640620, 20608, '<td valign="top">Cracking shot William, what a beautiful place</td>', 'Cracking shot William, what a beautiful place', '2008-02-08 14:19:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471371, 633145, 71455, '<td valign="top">Great Shot! I love the contrast in the clouds. I''d see about editing the cranes in the bottom right out of the photo though, there a little distracting.</td>', 'Great Shot! I love the contrast in the clouds. I''d see about editing the cranes in the bottom right out of the photo though, there a little distracting.', '2008-02-08 14:40:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471376, 640328, 62511, '<td valign="top">Poli erea photographia!</td>', 'Poli erea photographia!', '2008-02-08 14:45:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471386, 640531, 9821, '<td valign="top">never heard of it ... gotta go find that now<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mpeters:</b></div><hr/><i>Did you use <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=15266" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">idnic </a>''s pimp da eyes tutorial? </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'never heard of it ... gotta go find that now Originally posted by mpeters:Did you use  idnic ''s pimp da eyes tutorial? ', '2008-02-08 14:54:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471400, 630611, 43714, '<td valign="top">I love this shot, just great!!</td>', 'I love this shot, just great!!', '2008-02-08 15:03:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471405, 638581, 61651, '<td valign="top">It''s got that nice slice of life feel to it.  B&amp;W is good, as is the framing with the arch.</td>', 'It''s got that nice slice of life feel to it.  B&W is good, as is the framing with the arch.', '2008-02-08 15:09:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471411, 638977, 61651, '<td valign="top">Got to agree with some of the commenters - the grain gives the shot an edginess that it really does not need.  The really sweet moment captured here might have been better served by a softer look, less gritty look.  Keep in mind all this is very subjective - more about how a shot "feels" than what it "should" be.</td>', 'Got to agree with some of the commenters - the grain gives the shot an edginess that it really does not need.  The really sweet moment captured here might have been better served by a softer look, less gritty look.  Keep in mind all this is very subjective - more about how a shot "feels" than what it "should" be.', '2008-02-08 15:13:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471412, 640035, 61651, '<td valign="top">A simple and direct shot, in all its odd juxtapositions.  Yeah, the powerline is annoying, but at least it had the decency to slope at the same angle as the sign frame! :)</td>', 'A simple and direct shot, in all its odd juxtapositions.  Yeah, the powerline is annoying, but at least it had the decency to slope at the same angle as the sign frame! :)', '2008-02-08 15:16:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471415, 640962, 68599, '<td valign="top">Underated!</td>', 'Underated!', '2008-02-08 15:19:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471417, 640854, 61651, '<td valign="top">Dang!  A little too early for Reflections without Mirrors. :)  This has a certain grace, a little loss of detail in the brighter spots, but overall an impressive capture.</td>', 'Dang!  A little too early for Reflections without Mirrors. :)  This has a certain grace, a little loss of detail in the brighter spots, but overall an impressive capture.', '2008-02-08 15:19:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471423, 637756, 39850, '<td valign="top"><i>Is</i> it a vase?  Or some type of strange multiple exposure photographic trickery?  I didn''t get to this while voting.  It''s interesting - sure looks like you got a kick out of it (good for you).</td>', 'Is it a vase?  Or some type of strange multiple exposure photographic trickery?  I didn''t get to this while voting.  It''s interesting - sure looks like you got a kick out of it (good for you).', '2008-02-08 15:23:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471426, 638581, 68504, '<td valign="top">Don''t know where to begin.  This is amazing, and truly worthy of your title, a rare and precious conjunction. It reminds me of those medieval portraits where the landscape is seen through a window or archway; that is to say the arrangement and perspective have classic overtones.  This is also a candid with a wealth of telling detail contained by the strong lower curve of light and upper dark arch melded with the OOF watcher. That you have achieved so much compositionally and tellingly (AND in portrait orientation) should relegate dpc-type niggles to the tiny box in which they belong.</td>', 'Don''t know where to begin.  This is amazing, and truly worthy of your title, a rare and precious conjunction. It reminds me of those medieval portraits where the landscape is seen through a window or archway; that is to say the arrangement and perspective have classic overtones.  This is also a candid with a wealth of telling detail contained by the strong lower curve of light and upper dark arch melded with the OOF watcher. That you have achieved so much compositionally and tellingly (AND in portrait orientation) should relegate dpc-type niggles to the tiny box in which they belong.', '2008-02-08 15:27:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471439, 640651, 61651, '<td valign="top">Really just one of those underappreciated shots, nothing really "wrong" with it.  Very strong geometrics and shot in a way that it appears to be rushing at you; plus I like that funky looking wood behind the framing, really adds interest.</td>', 'Really just one of those underappreciated shots, nothing really "wrong" with it.  Very strong geometrics and shot in a way that it appears to be rushing at you; plus I like that funky looking wood behind the framing, really adds interest.', '2008-02-08 15:36:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471441, 638977, 68504, '<td valign="top">This has a very sweet and classic immediacy. The strength is in the two almost sketched faces; but I think the background of checked cushion and the bright line/cord behind the woman''s head seriously interfere with our enjoyment.  Overall balance and composition spot on.</td>', 'This has a very sweet and classic immediacy. The strength is in the two almost sketched faces; but I think the background of checked cushion and the bright line/cord behind the woman''s head seriously interfere with our enjoyment.  Overall balance and composition spot on.', '2008-02-08 15:37:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471443, 638552, 61651, '<td valign="top">Bokeh is attractive, colors and tones are appropriately wintery - I like what I see here. :)</td>', 'Bokeh is attractive, colors and tones are appropriately wintery - I like what I see here. :)', '2008-02-08 15:38:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471453, 640035, 68504, '<td valign="top">I really need to see more focus/detail in the building/stuff/detritus.  Overall, I like the brightness and for sure the quirkiness.</td>', 'I really need to see more focus/detail in the building/stuff/detritus.  Overall, I like the brightness and for sure the quirkiness.', '2008-02-08 15:43:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471486, 640398, 90032, '<td valign="top">I always loved the Northern lights, and this picture is one of the better images of them I''ve seen in a while. <br/> <br/>awesome job 10/10</td>', 'I always loved the Northern lights, and this picture is one of the better images of them I''ve seen in a while.  awesome job 10/10', '2008-02-08 15:56:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471515, 638137, 33068, '<td valign="top">Holy Cow!  Freaking awesome work.  Adding to favs for sure.<br/> <br/>A<br/> <br/>btw...Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Holy Cow!  Freaking awesome work.  Adding to favs for sure. A btw...Congrats on the ribbon.', '2008-02-08 16:15:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471529, 640596, 32345, '<td valign="top">All your hummingbird pictures are excellent Ann. They really deserves the high scores you got with them.<br/> <br/>Well done.</td>', 'All your hummingbird pictures are excellent Ann. They really deserves the high scores you got with them. Well done.', '2008-02-08 16:25:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471530, 634908, 68504, '<td valign="top">Framing, subject and action all good. Unfortunately the leaping forelegs are not very well defined against the albeit nicely rendered background which in these crucial areas is too busy.  Magnificent beast.</td>', 'Framing, subject and action all good. Unfortunately the leaping forelegs are not very well defined against the albeit nicely rendered background which in these crucial areas is too busy.  Magnificent beast.', '2008-02-08 16:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471574, 640852, 42013, '<td valign="top">Nice shot Neil and congrats!</td>', 'Nice shot Neil and congrats!', '2008-02-08 16:56:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471579, 640430, 43073, '<td valign="top">There are so many ghosts here. Ghosts don''t do well on DPC; people don''t like to see ghosts, it brings up too many of their own. But there are so many here. In the TV -- it''s not plugged in, I looked for the power cable, but it''s not there. So, either the picture is a ghost, or the tv is a ghost, showing images without electricity. And then there are the ghosts in the windows of the house. Ghosts of a place where everyone has been, but no one lives. I love your work, but just remember, not so many ghosts next time. Ghosts don''t do well on DPC . . .</td>', 'There are so many ghosts here. Ghosts don''t do well on DPC; people don''t like to see ghosts, it brings up too many of their own. But there are so many here. In the TV -- it''s not plugged in, I looked for the power cable, but it''s not there. So, either the picture is a ghost, or the tv is a ghost, showing images without electricity. And then there are the ghosts in the windows of the house. Ghosts of a place where everyone has been, but no one lives. I love your work, but just remember, not so many ghosts next time. Ghosts don''t do well on DPC . . .', '2008-02-08 17:01:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471584, 638112, 62318, '<td valign="top">Very nice effect and very ingenious. I was one of yor 8''s in the challenge. Though it was well done.</td>', 'Very nice effect and very ingenious. I was one of yor 8''s in the challenge. Though it was well done.', '2008-02-08 17:03:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471592, 640534, 43073, '<td valign="top">Such soft light, but even better, such wonderful shadows, hidden here and there. Under the boat, in the clouds at the horizon. You really have to search, but they''re there, with secrets, and memories, and just a tiny hint of anger. I hope it''s not me they''re angry with . . .. Delightful earth tones throughout here, wonderfully composed, wonderfully seen scene, and yes, a respectable score that still shows it wasn''t fully appreciated. More people need to look for the shadows.</td>', 'Such soft light, but even better, such wonderful shadows, hidden here and there. Under the boat, in the clouds at the horizon. You really have to search, but they''re there, with secrets, and memories, and just a tiny hint of anger. I hope it''s not me they''re angry with . . .. Delightful earth tones throughout here, wonderfully composed, wonderfully seen scene, and yes, a respectable score that still shows it wasn''t fully appreciated. More people need to look for the shadows.', '2008-02-08 17:07:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471595, 638823, 43073, '<td valign="top">I''m not in your group, and you already know what I think of this, but I have to say it anyway. It sings to me when I see it, a lovely melody, without a hint of discordance, without a hint of tonal flaws. It just sings, and I love its song.</td>', 'I''m not in your group, and you already know what I think of this, but I have to say it anyway. It sings to me when I see it, a lovely melody, without a hint of discordance, without a hint of tonal flaws. It just sings, and I love its song.', '2008-02-08 17:11:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471611, 640693, 11769, '<td valign="top">Beautiful. I voted this a 7 so I like very much.</td>', 'Beautiful. I voted this a 7 so I like very much.', '2008-02-08 17:20:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471613, 640852, 19178, '<td valign="top">Neil,  this is a great example of HDR!  Congratulations.</td>', 'Neil,  this is a great example of HDR!  Congratulations.', '2008-02-08 17:21:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471618, 631978, 1024, '<td valign="top">I love the vibrant colors on this bird, and I too am amazed about how close you got. He is looking directly at you and the eye contact is the nicest thing about this photo. It appears that you might have a little camera shake but that is not too surprising at 1/60.</td>', 'I love the vibrant colors on this bird, and I too am amazed about how close you got. He is looking directly at you and the eye contact is the nicest thing about this photo. It appears that you might have a little camera shake but that is not too surprising at 1/60.', '2008-02-08 17:25:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471619, 633148, 11769, '<td valign="top">Nice textures and color. Not something I feel that would score high in a DPC challenge but it sure is beautiful and sad.</td>', 'Nice textures and color. Not something I feel that would score high in a DPC challenge but it sure is beautiful and sad.', '2008-02-08 17:25:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471632, 640059, 11769, '<td valign="top">Neat how the water seems to be coming from nowhere. The upper branches and bushes took away from the beauty for me, they have a haphazard look I think. Still I gave you a 6 for the wonderful flowing water.</td>', 'Neat how the water seems to be coming from nowhere. The upper branches and bushes took away from the beauty for me, they have a haphazard look I think. Still I gave you a 6 for the wonderful flowing water.', '2008-02-08 17:32:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471634, 640398, 39850, '<td valign="top">Didn''t get to this one during voting, but it <i>is</i> amazing, as are all the shots I see on DPC of the <a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aurora_%28astronomy%29" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Aurora Borealis</a>, especially yours.  I really like that dead straight line you''ve included in this and the way the aurora is fanning across that incredible starry night sky.  Thank you for sharing these images and good to hear you never tire of them.  An image of this is one thing but to see this in person, especially the first time, must be literally breathtaking.  In imagining being there, I wonder --- just how cold is it out there in the middle of the night?</td>', 'Didn''t get to this one during voting, but it is amazing, as are all the shots I see on DPC of the Aurora Borealis, especially yours.  I really like that dead straight line you''ve included in this and the way the aurora is fanning across that incredible starry night sky.  Thank you for sharing these images and good to hear you never tire of them.  An image of this is one thing but to see this in person, especially the first time, must be literally breathtaking.  In imagining being there, I wonder --- just how cold is it out there in the middle of the night?', '2008-02-08 17:33:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471639, 640430, 44877, '<td valign="top">You''d think something unusual and quirky would be appreciated, but no. Love the composition, the sum of the elements in the photo and the tones. My only reservation would be the frame, which to me seems a little heavy in face of the soft colors of the image.<br/> <br/>Edit to say -  I just saw that you mentioned the frame yourself in the I love my shot thread. So nevermind.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 17:37:47.</i></td>', 'You''d think something unusual and quirky would be appreciated, but no. Love the composition, the sum of the elements in the photo and the tones. My only reservation would be the frame, which to me seems a little heavy in face of the soft colors of the image. Edit to say -  I just saw that you mentioned the frame yourself in the I love my shot thread. So nevermind.', '2008-02-08 17:37:02.000000', '2008-02-08 17:37:47.000000', 0),
(4471645, 638581, 44877, '<td valign="top">Fantastic street scene - the haze, the arch, all the different people - very well seen. Love the BW for this. It''s technically sound, clear, good contrast. Really excellent photo.</td>', 'Fantastic street scene - the haze, the arch, all the different people - very well seen. Love the BW for this. It''s technically sound, clear, good contrast. Really excellent photo.', '2008-02-08 17:40:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471650, 640854, 7743, '<td valign="top">I think you have a good idea here and high key can work.  A couple of things that I think let it down though.<br/> <br/>1) The water at the top of the shot - to me doesn''t add anything.  You could safely crop it out.<br/>2) The head of the bird is too dark.  Bring out the shadows on the head and I think you''d have a killer shot in conjunction with 1).<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 17:42:41.</i></td>', 'I think you have a good idea here and high key can work.  A couple of things that I think let it down though. 1) The water at the top of the shot - to me doesn''t add anything.  You could safely crop it out.2) The head of the bird is too dark.  Bring out the shadows on the head and I think you''d have a killer shot in conjunction with 1).', '2008-02-08 17:42:07.000000', '2008-02-08 17:42:41.000000', 0),
(4471664, 638552, 44877, '<td valign="top">The elements of the shot are wonderful - branch, berries, bokeh. Colors are really great. I''ll echo what some others said in terms of what is "off" - the rhythm or flow of the composition. A tighter crop, different angle for the DOF - something along those lines. The eye is unsure where to go. I think in a different challenge it would have done much better.</td>', 'The elements of the shot are wonderful - branch, berries, bokeh. Colors are really great. I''ll echo what some others said in terms of what is "off" - the rhythm or flow of the composition. A tighter crop, different angle for the DOF - something along those lines. The eye is unsure where to go. I think in a different challenge it would have done much better.', '2008-02-08 17:47:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471668, 640703, 44877, '<td valign="top">High contrast - people either love it or hate it. Here, the mostly hate it. <br/> <br/>I like this for its boldness and contrast, use of negative space and the composition overall. Well seen and interestingly processed.</td>', 'High contrast - people either love it or hate it. Here, the mostly hate it.  I like this for its boldness and contrast, use of negative space and the composition overall. Well seen and interestingly processed.', '2008-02-08 17:50:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471673, 640231, 44877, '<td valign="top">I really like the subdued colors in this shot. The repetition of tattoo motifs (on the neck, the arm, the wall) is awesome. Nice, tight crop - excellent. I''m sure it didn''t get a higher score because there is no wow- or aw-factor. It''s "just" an interesting, good candid.</td>', 'I really like the subdued colors in this shot. The repetition of tattoo motifs (on the neck, the arm, the wall) is awesome. Nice, tight crop - excellent. I''m sure it didn''t get a higher score because there is no wow- or aw-factor. It''s "just" an interesting, good candid.', '2008-02-08 17:53:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471676, 638823, 44877, '<td valign="top">Dang, that''s pretty. So delicate and interesting. Love, love, love the tones. It has an old-time feel to it, too. You were truly robbed. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Dang, that''s pretty. So delicate and interesting. Love, love, love the tones. It has an old-time feel to it, too. You were truly robbed.  ', '2008-02-08 17:58:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471681, 640693, 1024, '<td valign="top">I loved this shot when I voted on this challenge.  I love the high key effect and the fact that you really can not tell what he is walking toward.  This is actually a really good score, and you should be proud.</td>', 'I loved this shot when I voted on this challenge.  I love the high key effect and the fact that you really can not tell what he is walking toward.  This is actually a really good score, and you should be proud.', '2008-02-08 18:02:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471686, 637396, 1024, '<td valign="top">I really loved this during voting.  You got a very respectable score,  and you should be proud of it.  Beautiful capture.</td>', 'I really loved this during voting.  You got a very respectable score,  and you should be proud of it.  Beautiful capture.', '2008-02-08 18:04:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471689, 640059, 1024, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful shot, and your score is not bad.  I think the branches did hurt you a little bit, bet this would be magnificent in the spring when everything is green rather than beige.</td>', 'This is a beautiful shot, and your score is not bad.  I think the branches did hurt you a little bit, bet this would be magnificent in the spring when everything is green rather than beige.', '2008-02-08 18:06:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471737, 639468, 53316, '<td valign="top">I think this shot''s perfect :-)</td>', 'I think this shot''s perfect :-)', '2008-02-08 18:30:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471773, 634908, 66384, '<td valign="top">I really like the subject, composition and colors. I think a Levels adjustment would improve the image, more contrast would help too. There is an USM action called Luko Sharpening that I think would add depth and vitality to the shot. That might also help the focus that seems to have fallen a little short. The rocks in front of the goat seem sharper than the goat itself. If you want the details of Luko sharpening, send me a PM.<br/> <br/>I think with a bit more work in Photoshop, you will have an impressive photo.</td>', 'I really like the subject, composition and colors. I think a Levels adjustment would improve the image, more contrast would help too. There is an USM action called Luko Sharpening that I think would add depth and vitality to the shot. That might also help the focus that seems to have fallen a little short. The rocks in front of the goat seem sharper than the goat itself. If you want the details of Luko sharpening, send me a PM. I think with a bit more work in Photoshop, you will have an impressive photo.', '2008-02-08 18:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471788, 639253, 62318, '<td valign="top">I really enjoyed this shot in the challenge. Gave you a 7. I thought it was a wonderful study of form and texture. Also has a very nice contrast. Probably just did not have that pop people were looking for, but in the case of this photo it is a much more telling shot the more you look at it.</td>', 'I really enjoyed this shot in the challenge. Gave you a 7. I thought it was a wonderful study of form and texture. Also has a very nice contrast. Probably just did not have that pop people were looking for, but in the case of this photo it is a much more telling shot the more you look at it.', '2008-02-08 18:51:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471795, 637396, 11769, '<td valign="top">Wonderful capture. The only nit pic would be to crop the left to make the image more centered, I think the illusion of space would still be there but my eye wouldn''t be drawn to the empty star field off to the left side. Nice one.</td>', 'Wonderful capture. The only nit pic would be to crop the left to make the image more centered, I think the illusion of space would still be there but my eye wouldn''t be drawn to the empty star field off to the left side. Nice one.', '2008-02-08 18:56:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471801, 640878, 62318, '<td valign="top">The only thing I might say is that perhaps the top left is a bit too bright, maybe just a little lower on the brightness up there. But maybe that is what you were going for to emphasize the divine or maybe your were going for diving rods. The rest of the photo for me at least is stunning. Wonderful contrasts and tones and terrific subjects. A shame that it scored so poorly.</td>', 'The only thing I might say is that perhaps the top left is a bit too bright, maybe just a little lower on the brightness up there. But maybe that is what you were going for to emphasize the divine or maybe your were going for diving rods. The rest of the photo for me at least is stunning. Wonderful contrasts and tones and terrific subjects. A shame that it scored so poorly.', '2008-02-08 18:58:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471809, 640401, 66384, '<td valign="top">People seemed to have liked this image -- the majority of the votes are six and above, and nobody trashed it with a one or two. I think it is just the distracting blown highlights on the right that prevented a really high score. The model is beautiful and you did a great job of capturing that beauty.<br/> <br/>You said the hair on the right was lost in the b&amp;w conversion. I''m wondering what method you used for the conversion, and I''m wondering if you could use two different layers with different parameters for the b&amp;w conversion. Then use masks to bring back the blown hair.</td>', 'People seemed to have liked this image -- the majority of the votes are six and above, and nobody trashed it with a one or two. I think it is just the distracting blown highlights on the right that prevented a really high score. The model is beautiful and you did a great job of capturing that beauty. You said the hair on the right was lost in the b&w conversion. I''m wondering what method you used for the conversion, and I''m wondering if you could use two different layers with different parameters for the b&w conversion. Then use masks to bring back the blown hair.', '2008-02-08 19:03:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471827, 638823, 66384, '<td valign="top">Oh, Karen, I love this image. I haven''t a clue what the problem it. You got a favorite too. I think without realizing it, Xuko has told you why it didn''t score as high as I think it deserved. There are probably a lot of voters who feel the same way he does.</td>', 'Oh, Karen, I love this image. I haven''t a clue what the problem it. You got a favorite too. I think without realizing it, Xuko has told you why it didn''t score as high as I think it deserved. There are probably a lot of voters who feel the same way he does.', '2008-02-08 19:12:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471840, 640401, 54843, '<td valign="top">I meant that the effect from my lighting is not as prominent when I convert to B&amp;W...and the white background further reduces the effect the lighting has on the image.  If the background were black...we would have a slightly different conversation...and the highlights would be even more distracting.</td>', 'I meant that the effect from my lighting is not as prominent when I convert to B&W...and the white background further reduces the effect the lighting has on the image.  If the background were black...we would have a slightly different conversation...and the highlights would be even more distracting.', '2008-02-08 19:18:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471847, 640401, 54843, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=644097" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/54843/120/644097.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/54843/120/644097.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/54843/120/644097.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>The original image.  As you can see...the hair is much more prominent in the color version.</td>', '  The original image.  As you can see...the hair is much more prominent in the color version.', '2008-02-08 19:23:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471852, 640231, 66384, '<td valign="top">I think your composition is good and the subject is interesting. I don''t have much insight to offer that hasn''t already been covered. I do know that the majority of voters don''t respond well to greenish casts on images. A couple of times I used a greenish tone intentionally, and both times I got slammed, and enough comments make it clear that they didn''t like the green tone. <br/> <br/>One thing that the others haven''t mentioned is that there is a very lot going on in this image. The voters like uncluttered, simple shots with a clear focal point that draws the eye. Maybe a shallower DOF focusing on the arm would have made this look less like a candid, and given the viewers a little more direction for their wandering eyes.<br/> <br/>BTW, I like it, and I like the big flower on the back of her head.</td>', 'I think your composition is good and the subject is interesting. I don''t have much insight to offer that hasn''t already been covered. I do know that the majority of voters don''t respond well to greenish casts on images. A couple of times I used a greenish tone intentionally, and both times I got slammed, and enough comments make it clear that they didn''t like the green tone.  One thing that the others haven''t mentioned is that there is a very lot going on in this image. The voters like uncluttered, simple shots with a clear focal point that draws the eye. Maybe a shallower DOF focusing on the arm would have made this look less like a candid, and given the viewers a little more direction for their wandering eyes. BTW, I like it, and I like the big flower on the back of her head.', '2008-02-08 19:27:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471860, 638112, 66384, '<td valign="top">I love it, Jelena. The more I look at it, I want to look at it more. I wish this had made it to your top row. The colors are spectacular.</td>', 'I love it, Jelena. The more I look at it, I want to look at it more. I wish this had made it to your top row. The colors are spectacular.', '2008-02-08 19:36:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471874, 640534, 66384, '<td valign="top">Once again, Terry, this is one of my favorites of the challenge. I never do guess which is yours, because you are so versatile. I think the processing on this is wonderful. I love the soft colors, and the composition is really good.</td>', 'Once again, Terry, this is one of my favorites of the challenge. I never do guess which is yours, because you are so versatile. I think the processing on this is wonderful. I love the soft colors, and the composition is really good.', '2008-02-08 19:42:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471891, 640854, 66384, '<td valign="top">This is so cool with the bird, shadow, and reflection all grouped so beautifully. The position of the bird is excellent, with the wing tips in the water. And I like the high key effect. Really nice image!</td>', 'This is so cool with the bird, shadow, and reflection all grouped so beautifully. The position of the bird is excellent, with the wing tips in the water. And I like the high key effect. Really nice image!', '2008-02-08 19:57:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471894, 640854, 65234, '<td valign="top">Like the high key processing and the shadow, and particularly like the wing position and the reflection.  It''s really cool that the wing, shadow and reflection all converge at the wingtips.  Really extraordinarily good angle and timing on your part.  I might dodge the face a bit to get more detail there and maybe crop a little tighter on the right and bottom so he''s not so centered, but the shot is certainly better than the score it got.</td>', 'Like the high key processing and the shadow, and particularly like the wing position and the reflection.  It''s really cool that the wing, shadow and reflection all converge at the wingtips.  Really extraordinarily good angle and timing on your part.  I might dodge the face a bit to get more detail there and maybe crop a little tighter on the right and bottom so he''s not so centered, but the shot is certainly better than the score it got.', '2008-02-08 20:01:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471908, 633148, 65234, '<td valign="top">I''m kind of amused that the UMW sign in the shot is still in perfect shape while the building crumbles around it.  Especially since it looks like that''s in the oldest part of the building.<br/> <br/>You''d think it being on the register of historic places would prompt someone to do something about it, but I guess no one thinks it''s worth the investment.  Rather sad.  I can see why you wanted to tell this story.</td>', 'I''m kind of amused that the UMW sign in the shot is still in perfect shape while the building crumbles around it.  Especially since it looks like that''s in the oldest part of the building. You''d think it being on the register of historic places would prompt someone to do something about it, but I guess no one thinks it''s worth the investment.  Rather sad.  I can see why you wanted to tell this story.', '2008-02-08 20:11:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471920, 631978, 65234, '<td valign="top">You''re right, the eye is sharp, but the beak isn''t.  He could have been in mid-chew; at f/8 it shouldn''t be a DOF issue.  I think people expect the eye and beak to have the same amount of sharpness since they''re usually the same distance from the lens, and either one being soft loses you points.  Plus there''s the added factor that some voters were probably tired of birds by the time they got to yours!<br/> <br/>I really like his position in the image and the eye contact is pretty darned cool.  You really did get phenomenal detail in that eyeball.</td>', 'You''re right, the eye is sharp, but the beak isn''t.  He could have been in mid-chew; at f/8 it shouldn''t be a DOF issue.  I think people expect the eye and beak to have the same amount of sharpness since they''re usually the same distance from the lens, and either one being soft loses you points.  Plus there''s the added factor that some voters were probably tired of birds by the time they got to yours! I really like his position in the image and the eye contact is pretty darned cool.  You really did get phenomenal detail in that eyeball.', '2008-02-08 20:18:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471928, 638581, 47483, '<td valign="top">This is a good and bad photo. Good photo in the respect that it tells a story, bad photo in the sense that it fails to make impact visually and lacks ability to hold the viewer. <br/>The probable reason for this might be is that the photo looks almost flat through out the frame. Stronger contrast might have helped.</td>', 'This is a good and bad photo. Good photo in the respect that it tells a story, bad photo in the sense that it fails to make impact visually and lacks ability to hold the viewer. The probable reason for this might be is that the photo looks almost flat through out the frame. Stronger contrast might have helped.', '2008-02-08 20:25:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471931, 640035, 1024, '<td valign="top">This photo has the perfect DOF to add to the "antique" background.  I also like the processing and the tones.  The one thing that is a little distracting to me are the tree branches over the building.  They  give a cluttered feel to the image.  <br/> <br/>But now that I have typed that, it seems that cluttered is sort of what this photo is all about.  Maybe that is what you were going for and nailed it absolutely.</td>', 'This photo has the perfect DOF to add to the "antique" background.  I also like the processing and the tones.  The one thing that is a little distracting to me are the tree branches over the building.  They  give a cluttered feel to the image.   But now that I have typed that, it seems that cluttered is sort of what this photo is all about.  Maybe that is what you were going for and nailed it absolutely.', '2008-02-08 20:26:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471933, 640872, 65234, '<td valign="top">Well, I''ll just throw another completely different opinion in here ;-)<br/> <br/>I Like the water and the rays you got from the sun, so I would crop out a lot of the sky and get the sun more or less in the upper right ROT position.  That makes the diagonal in the clouds more distinct by cropping out most of the amorphous one on the right, and also emphasizes the diagonal reflection of the clouds in the water so everything kind of converges toward the right horizon.</td>', 'Well, I''ll just throw another completely different opinion in here ;-) I Like the water and the rays you got from the sun, so I would crop out a lot of the sky and get the sun more or less in the upper right ROT position.  That makes the diagonal in the clouds more distinct by cropping out most of the amorphous one on the right, and also emphasizes the diagonal reflection of the clouds in the water so everything kind of converges toward the right horizon.', '2008-02-08 20:28:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471936, 638977, 47483, '<td valign="top">First of all sorry for not repling your PM, i am just too tied up with things around me, life is being little turbulent. <br/> <br/><i>One of my lowest scoring images here at DPC over the years, but I still like it and don''t regret anything except maybe the decision to add grain. May reconsider that next time. :-P </i> <br/> <br/>In my opinion it is the grain that makes this picture and creates the mood. Don''t take the scores to heart, DPC being populated by photographers mainly the technicals overpower their decision making while voting but there are people like me who try to think photographs as moments of life we wish to keep with us. This is one of such photographs.</td>', 'First of all sorry for not repling your PM, i am just too tied up with things around me, life is being little turbulent.  One of my lowest scoring images here at DPC over the years, but I still like it and don''t regret anything except maybe the decision to add grain. May reconsider that next time. :-P   In my opinion it is the grain that makes this picture and creates the mood. Don''t take the scores to heart, DPC being populated by photographers mainly the technicals overpower their decision making while voting but there are people like me who try to think photographs as moments of life we wish to keep with us. This is one of such photographs.', '2008-02-08 20:29:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471940, 640035, 47483, '<td valign="top">BW conversion was good and probably the strongest point of this. But I am sorry to say I do not find it interesting. And this is probably undoing of this photo. I really did not like the framing. Sorry for being negative but this is how I felt.</td>', 'BW conversion was good and probably the strongest point of this. But I am sorry to say I do not find it interesting. And this is probably undoing of this photo. I really did not like the framing. Sorry for being negative but this is how I felt.', '2008-02-08 20:32:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471948, 638290, 67697, '<td valign="top">I do love this.  The hair is wild!  Such a sweet smirk too.  I like a lot about the processing too.  Love the black and white background and the vignette.  Too bad this did not score higher.</td>', 'I do love this.  The hair is wild!  Such a sweet smirk too.  I like a lot about the processing too.  Love the black and white background and the vignette.  Too bad this did not score higher.', '2008-02-08 20:40:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471949, 640430, 83313, '<td valign="top">When I voted/commented on this one the first time, I have to admit that I did not pay careful enough attention, and did not realize there was that reflection in the screen that looked like it was turned on. I think a lot of people in their haste to vote on a lot of pictures missed that subtlety. <br/> <br/>I think the image itself is a little deadpan, and a lot of voters (myself included) didn''t get it. I don''t know if that description makes sense or not. But, as I had said during my in-voting comment, I  did not think this one would have broad appeal.</td>', 'When I voted/commented on this one the first time, I have to admit that I did not pay careful enough attention, and did not realize there was that reflection in the screen that looked like it was turned on. I think a lot of people in their haste to vote on a lot of pictures missed that subtlety.  I think the image itself is a little deadpan, and a lot of voters (myself included) didn''t get it. I don''t know if that description makes sense or not. But, as I had said during my in-voting comment, I  did not think this one would have broad appeal.', '2008-02-08 20:41:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471956, 634256, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is a very interesting catch.  I love how you used the green and white to pop out from your bokeh background.  I think I would have liked to see a little more focus on the entire branch since it''s color is prominent like the part that is in focus.  This is a beautiful find!</td>', 'This is a very interesting catch.  I love how you used the green and white to pop out from your bokeh background.  I think I would have liked to see a little more focus on the entire branch since it''s color is prominent like the part that is in focus.  This is a beautiful find!', '2008-02-08 20:45:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471957, 640534, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nice enhancement to the look of those clouds. You came within spitting distance of a 6 on this one!<br/> <br/>Biggest issue I can see that may have held it back is the hulls of the boats blend in with the beach colors too much, so the eye does wanders between the boats and the scene out in the water behind them.</td>', 'Nice enhancement to the look of those clouds. You came within spitting distance of a 6 on this one! Biggest issue I can see that may have held it back is the hulls of the boats blend in with the beach colors too much, so the eye does wanders between the boats and the scene out in the water behind them.', '2008-02-08 20:45:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471958, 640854, 47483, '<td valign="top">Well you did not go to extremes , here is the extreme processing. <br/>[thumb]644128[/thumb]<br/> <br/>I liked your version though since that is simple and good. But this is its problem simple and good do not sell well at DPC. Here perfect and extraordinary with lots of WOW works well.</td>', 'Well you did not go to extremes , here is the extreme processing. [thumb]644128[/thumb] I liked your version though since that is simple and good. But this is its problem simple and good do not sell well at DPC. Here perfect and extraordinary with lots of WOW works well.', '2008-02-08 20:45:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471961, 638264, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is so bizarre - so I like it, of course.  I like the grass blanket.  I''m disappointed that you did not give more background info here.  So what''s the story?</td>', 'This is so bizarre - so I like it, of course.  I like the grass blanket.  I''m disappointed that you did not give more background info here.  So what''s the story?', '2008-02-08 20:46:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471967, 631978, 83313, '<td valign="top">I don''t think out of focus or dpeth of field was really the problem. Though his eye is nice and sharp, the beak looks like there was some motion blur going on. I the beak were as clear as the area behind it, I don''t think the rest of it would have been as big a problem, but my eye is drawn to the blurry beak.</td>', 'I don''t think out of focus or dpeth of field was really the problem. Though his eye is nice and sharp, the beak looks like there was some motion blur going on. I the beak were as clear as the area behind it, I don''t think the rest of it would have been as big a problem, but my eye is drawn to the blurry beak.', '2008-02-08 20:50:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471969, 640974, 47483, '<td valign="top">First thanks for your comments I value them a lot. <br/>Second pet pictures are not my cup of tea so for me its difficult to make any comments on it. <br/>The only reason that I could think why it did bad is that it was in free study and against lots of very good work. Here someone has to come to bottom.</td>', 'First thanks for your comments I value them a lot. Second pet pictures are not my cup of tea so for me its difficult to make any comments on it. The only reason that I could think why it did bad is that it was in free study and against lots of very good work. Here someone has to come to bottom.', '2008-02-08 20:50:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471973, 640942, 65234, '<td valign="top">Doinking?!  That''s some unique PP program you''ve got there, mister.<br/> <br/>The scene is lovely, no question.  I would like to see more of the detail on the house, just ''cuz I LOVE stone houses.  Lots of character.  I wonder, too, if the sidewalk was also stone, and should show more of the brown color of the house?  The driveway is not as good a leading line with snow all over it.  Also might see what I could get if I stepped up a few feet so that little tree on the left wasn''t in the shot.  But then you might lose the cannon, and living in VA I appreciate seeing the occasional cannon in someone''s front yard :-)</td>', 'Doinking?!  That''s some unique PP program you''ve got there, mister. The scene is lovely, no question.  I would like to see more of the detail on the house, just ''cuz I LOVE stone houses.  Lots of character.  I wonder, too, if the sidewalk was also stone, and should show more of the brown color of the house?  The driveway is not as good a leading line with snow all over it.  Also might see what I could get if I stepped up a few feet so that little tree on the left wasn''t in the shot.  But then you might lose the cannon, and living in VA I appreciate seeing the occasional cannon in someone''s front yard :-)', '2008-02-08 20:52:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471975, 639327, 67697, '<td valign="top">You have such a great ability to find interesting people for your shots.  He kinda looks like Wesley Snipes.  Of course, if it was him, I guess it would not surprise me.  Interesting portrait of a snappy dresser.</td>', 'You have such a great ability to find interesting people for your shots.  He kinda looks like Wesley Snipes.  Of course, if it was him, I guess it would not surprise me.  Interesting portrait of a snappy dresser.', '2008-02-08 20:53:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471976, 640854, 83313, '<td valign="top">I think the extreme brightness in the upper half of the frame is what held this back a little. I woudl have also cropped it a bit differently, placing the bird a bit more to the right. I do like the reflection of the bird in the wet sand and darkening the image would also bring that out a little more.</td>', 'I think the extreme brightness in the upper half of the frame is what held this back a little. I woudl have also cropped it a bit differently, placing the bird a bit more to the right. I do like the reflection of the bird in the wet sand and darkening the image would also bring that out a little more.', '2008-02-08 20:54:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471979, 640854, 68504, '<td valign="top">First off, an astonishing capture of pose and position on shallows, including both shadow and reflection.  Processing brings this totally to the fore.  But it also puts you in a tricky position of having to coordinate these 3 features, which compete for my attention and focus.  I don''t know if different framing or colour adjustment (black and white) would help. And oh, those wingtips!</td>', 'First off, an astonishing capture of pose and position on shallows, including both shadow and reflection.  Processing brings this totally to the fore.  But it also puts you in a tricky position of having to coordinate these 3 features, which compete for my attention and focus.  I don''t know if different framing or colour adjustment (black and white) would help. And oh, those wingtips!', '2008-02-08 20:59:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471980, 638823, 67697, '<td valign="top">Oooh how much fun are you going to have with an IR camera?  I don''t know much about what a picture looks like straight from the camera but I wanted to say that on my screen, this one looks like it has a hint of reddish-purplish color.  This is interesting with the specks of dark bulbs.  I''ve seen some really cool plant shots done with IR so I look forward to seeing what you are going to do!</td>', 'Oooh how much fun are you going to have with an IR camera?  I don''t know much about what a picture looks like straight from the camera but I wanted to say that on my screen, this one looks like it has a hint of reddish-purplish color.  This is interesting with the specks of dark bulbs.  I''ve seen some really cool plant shots done with IR so I look forward to seeing what you are going to do!', '2008-02-08 21:00:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471981, 637789, 67697, '<td valign="top">lol this looks like some kind of baseball park shot with the lights there.  You have baseball in your blood for sure.  I love how the lights are reaching up into that strong, contrasty sky.  The blues are beautiful!</td>', 'lol this looks like some kind of baseball park shot with the lights there.  You have baseball in your blood for sure.  I love how the lights are reaching up into that strong, contrasty sky.  The blues are beautiful!', '2008-02-08 21:02:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471983, 632908, 83313, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this one, but I would have probably given it a 5. The composition is pretty good. I think the main issue is the clarity of the image as a whole, and a bit of graininess. The 1/20 second exposure may have had something to do with that. Were you using a tripod? If it was handheld, then I admire your ability to hold a camera steady at that shutter speed. I would have probably bumped up the colors a touch to bring out the rosy cheeks, sparkly eyes and the bokeh in the back.<br/> <br/>I think to some extent it was a little out of season right now and some voters may have viewed it as a photo of someone else''s piece of art.</td>', 'I didn''t vote on this one, but I would have probably given it a 5. The composition is pretty good. I think the main issue is the clarity of the image as a whole, and a bit of graininess. The 1/20 second exposure may have had something to do with that. Were you using a tripod? If it was handheld, then I admire your ability to hold a camera steady at that shutter speed. I would have probably bumped up the colors a touch to bring out the rosy cheeks, sparkly eyes and the bokeh in the back. I think to some extent it was a little out of season right now and some voters may have viewed it as a photo of someone else''s piece of art.', '2008-02-08 21:03:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471986, 640490, 68504, '<td valign="top">Pretty much what <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30049" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">glad2badad</a> said, especially about your photo''s strengths.</td>', 'Pretty much what  glad2badad said, especially about your photo''s strengths.', '2008-02-08 21:06:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471987, 638552, 65234, '<td valign="top">Oooh, great minds think alike <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=634815" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/801/120/634815.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/801/120/634815.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/801/120/634815.jpg"/></a>.  Same title, even!  <br/> <br/>Mine didn''t do exceptionally well in its challenge, either, so my opinion might not help much.  I love your colors, bokeh and DOF, but I do tend to like angled compositions better.</td>', 'Oooh, great minds think alike .  Same title, even!   Mine didn''t do exceptionally well in its challenge, either, so my opinion might not help much.  I love your colors, bokeh and DOF, but I do tend to like angled compositions better.', '2008-02-08 21:06:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471989, 637397, 67697, '<td valign="top">Did you use some of that Lucis Arts stuff?  The processing is interesting here.  What a sweet jowly face.  I love how she is dressed for play.  The ears flying like that is pretty cool too.</td>', 'Did you use some of that Lucis Arts stuff?  The processing is interesting here.  What a sweet jowly face.  I love how she is dressed for play.  The ears flying like that is pretty cool too.', '2008-02-08 21:07:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471992, 640506, 67697, '<td valign="top">I wonder why this is a sub-5 shot?  It''s clear, the subject is in focus, the blue colortone is gorgeous, the angle adds interest.  I didn''t get to it during voting so i''m not sure what I would have given it - at least a 6 for sure.  I don''t really get moved by architecture shots, but I''d say that you have a very good one here.  Shame it was not appreciated more.</td>', 'I wonder why this is a sub-5 shot?  It''s clear, the subject is in focus, the blue colortone is gorgeous, the angle adds interest.  I didn''t get to it during voting so i''m not sure what I would have given it - at least a 6 for sure.  I don''t really get moved by architecture shots, but I''d say that you have a very good one here.  Shame it was not appreciated more.', '2008-02-08 21:11:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4471995, 640651, 65234, '<td valign="top">This is not the kind of shot I can scroll up and down to see if I like a different crop!  It''s making me dizzy even when it''s not moving ::yikes::  I think it''s the wood pattern radiating behind the white woodwork.  It''s really quite fascinating to look at.<br/> <br/>Don''t know why it didn''t do better; maybe you just made it look too easy to get!</td>', 'This is not the kind of shot I can scroll up and down to see if I like a different crop!  It''s making me dizzy even when it''s not moving ::yikes::  I think it''s the wood pattern radiating behind the white woodwork.  It''s really quite fascinating to look at. Don''t know why it didn''t do better; maybe you just made it look too easy to get!', '2008-02-08 21:14:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472001, 639497, 65234, '<td valign="top">Hmm.  Pretty scene and lovely blue to the sky.  I like the mountains.  The crop does feel like there''s a bit too much sky because the clouds are not very dramatic.  I think I would like to see more detail in the foreground.  Not tons, but a little.  It''s too solid and dark for the rest of the scene IMO.</td>', 'Hmm.  Pretty scene and lovely blue to the sky.  I like the mountains.  The crop does feel like there''s a bit too much sky because the clouds are not very dramatic.  I think I would like to see more detail in the foreground.  Not tons, but a little.  It''s too solid and dark for the rest of the scene IMO.', '2008-02-08 21:17:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472003, 632908, 61651, '<td valign="top">I like how the bokeh seems like just larger twinkles that match the twinkles in his eyes.  I don''t know if you shot this handheld or not, but at 1/20s it may have been too slow for handheld, to avoid softness due to hand shake.  Also the aperture might have been too wide -  I think what could have led to some of the poorer votes were the parts of the shot that fall out of focus, like the beard and eyebrows, which a greater depth of field may have helped.  With such a narrow DOF, critical focus is even more critical, and anything, like handshake at slower shutter speeds, will be even more dramatically apparent.  Of course if you didn''t intend the beard and eyebrows to be in focus, my comment is irrelevant - I''m a big believer in the photographer''s intent trumping what any particular viewer might "want" from your image. :)  <br/> <br/>In any case, votes below 4 for this image seem harsh.  Personally I voted this a 5, which means to me a shot that is decent but just doesn''t particularly "grab" me.</td>', 'I like how the bokeh seems like just larger twinkles that match the twinkles in his eyes.  I don''t know if you shot this handheld or not, but at 1/20s it may have been too slow for handheld, to avoid softness due to hand shake.  Also the aperture might have been too wide -  I think what could have led to some of the poorer votes were the parts of the shot that fall out of focus, like the beard and eyebrows, which a greater depth of field may have helped.  With such a narrow DOF, critical focus is even more critical, and anything, like handshake at slower shutter speeds, will be even more dramatically apparent.  Of course if you didn''t intend the beard and eyebrows to be in focus, my comment is irrelevant - I''m a big believer in the photographer''s intent trumping what any particular viewer might "want" from your image. :)   In any case, votes below 4 for this image seem harsh.  Personally I voted this a 5, which means to me a shot that is decent but just doesn''t particularly "grab" me.', '2008-02-08 21:23:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472004, 640974, 47483, '<td valign="top">Yaa that could be my monitor too. <br/>I just bumped up everything to see how it would look. <br/> <br/>High contrast are difficult sell. <br/>Look at this:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=620576" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/784/120/620576.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/784/120/620576.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/784/120/620576.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-08 21:26:54.</i></td>', 'Yaa that could be my monitor too. I just bumped up everything to see how it would look.  High contrast are difficult sell. Look at this:', '2008-02-08 21:25:47.000000', '2008-02-08 21:26:54.000000', 0),
(4472005, 631825, 65234, '<td valign="top">I like the subject, but I think there is a little too much detail in the background and it takes away from the cars.  Getting closer or using a shallower DOF might make them stand out better.  Or, crop out most of what is above the fence to emphasize the cars and weeds.  Maybe play with dodge and burn to make them stand out more, too.</td>', 'I like the subject, but I think there is a little too much detail in the background and it takes away from the cars.  Getting closer or using a shallower DOF might make them stand out better.  Or, crop out most of what is above the fence to emphasize the cars and weeds.  Maybe play with dodge and burn to make them stand out more, too.', '2008-02-08 21:26:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472011, 640637, 61651, '<td valign="top">My first impression of this shot is RED - nice brilliant color, with good contrast against the deep blue in the sky.  My second impression is that the composition overall seems a bit constrictive to me, like there''s not enough room for your subject to breath.  I think your choice of shooting angle does this, mostly - point and shoots usually have a fairly wide angle lens, 26mm or so if I''m not mistaken (and I very well could be mistaken!), but that may not have been wide enough to fully exploit your shooting angle and give a nice sense of breadth to the car''s grill.</td>', 'My first impression of this shot is RED - nice brilliant color, with good contrast against the deep blue in the sky.  My second impression is that the composition overall seems a bit constrictive to me, like there''s not enough room for your subject to breath.  I think your choice of shooting angle does this, mostly - point and shoots usually have a fairly wide angle lens, 26mm or so if I''m not mistaken (and I very well could be mistaken!), but that may not have been wide enough to fully exploit your shooting angle and give a nice sense of breadth to the car''s grill.', '2008-02-08 21:30:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472079, 640398, 84178, '<td valign="top">Good for you shooting these pics.. for you. Stay with it they are beautiful.  I am a single mom and do very little but it is a hobby.. So goodluck and keep up the good work.</td>', 'Good for you shooting these pics.. for you. Stay with it they are beautiful.  I am a single mom and do very little but it is a hobby.. So goodluck and keep up the good work.', '2008-02-08 22:11:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472083, 640651, 80976, '<td valign="top">This pic has definite potential.<br/> <br/>Methinks you should go back there late at night with a flashlight so you can paint it and make that wood really pop.</td>', 'This pic has definite potential. Methinks you should go back there late at night with a flashlight so you can paint it and make that wood really pop.', '2008-02-08 22:14:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472189, 635266, 43031, '<td valign="top">This is simply awesome Andi. Maybe I need to get some more pain to get some more gain too ;)</td>', 'This is simply awesome Andi. Maybe I need to get some more pain to get some more gain too ;)', '2008-02-08 23:39:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472295, 640852, 86964, '<td valign="top">Wow... absolutely amazing shot...  this should be put in a frame!!</td>', 'Wow... absolutely amazing shot...  this should be put in a frame!!', '2008-02-09 00:24:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472308, 637396, 9668, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image, great composition and lighting. I have <a href="//gallery.ecola.us/thumbnails.php?album=search&amp;search=jellyfish" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">shot jellyfish before</a> and know it is hard to get an good image that is in focus, well lit, and with a relatively good composition. You''ve done quite well here. I like the white specs in the background. I think you chose the correct image to submit compared to your two outtakes.</td>', 'Beautiful image, great composition and lighting. I have shot jellyfish before and know it is hard to get an good image that is in focus, well lit, and with a relatively good composition. You''ve done quite well here. I like the white specs in the background. I think you chose the correct image to submit compared to your two outtakes.', '2008-02-09 00:29:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472322, 640569, 22301, '<td valign="top">this is one of those real images that can sometimes slip through the cracks. should have been atleast a 6!</td>', 'this is one of those real images that can sometimes slip through the cracks. should have been atleast a 6!', '2008-02-09 00:32:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472332, 640693, 9668, '<td valign="top">Lovely artistic shot! Not entirely sure about the gray vignetting around the edges. Maybe it makes it more interesting, but it kinda distracts me too. idk. I like how the foot steps lead up. When I first saw this image, I got the impression that the person was floating somehow...then I connected the footprints and snow =). Grainyness doesn''t bother me much, but in this image, I can only find the grainyness on the back of the figure, that''s bothersome to me. I was going to say something about the objects faded in the background, but I found that I like them, they give the image more depth.</td>', 'Lovely artistic shot! Not entirely sure about the gray vignetting around the edges. Maybe it makes it more interesting, but it kinda distracts me too. idk. I like how the foot steps lead up. When I first saw this image, I got the impression that the person was floating somehow...then I connected the footprints and snow =). Grainyness doesn''t bother me much, but in this image, I can only find the grainyness on the back of the figure, that''s bothersome to me. I was going to say something about the objects faded in the background, but I found that I like them, they give the image more depth.', '2008-02-09 00:36:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472339, 640398, 31637, '<td valign="top">Forget the people who are sick of borealis photos, keep taking these photos! I could look at them all day long, keep up the good work.</td>', 'Forget the people who are sick of borealis photos, keep taking these photos! I could look at them all day long, keep up the good work.', '2008-02-09 00:45:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472370, 631978, 9668, '<td valign="top">Nice picture of a cardinal (and I love cardinals). Doesn''t quite have the technical aspects and wow factor DPC likes though. First off, yeah, the image is relatively sharp, but not tack sharp. The composition is well, sorry to say, kind of boring. It is all centered. My eye is immediately drawn to the eye of the bird, but there isn''t much to look at after that. I would like to see a little bit deeper DOF, but it looks like that''d be hard to do with this bird and those lighting conditions. Still, impressively close shot of a cardinal.</td>', 'Nice picture of a cardinal (and I love cardinals). Doesn''t quite have the technical aspects and wow factor DPC likes though. First off, yeah, the image is relatively sharp, but not tack sharp. The composition is well, sorry to say, kind of boring. It is all centered. My eye is immediately drawn to the eye of the bird, but there isn''t much to look at after that. I would like to see a little bit deeper DOF, but it looks like that''d be hard to do with this bird and those lighting conditions. Still, impressively close shot of a cardinal.', '2008-02-09 01:15:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472371, 633148, 9668, '<td valign="top">Nice picture of this hotel (specially compared to some that I saw in that historical link. cool to see it before though). I think one of the big problems of this shot, especially for DPC isn''t extremely interesting to look at...it doesn''t have the DPC "wow" factor. I think it is interesting to look at, especially with the vibrant colors and depth you''ve captured, but it is basically a picture of decaying hotel. I think it''d be cool to see somebody inside it looking around, but maybe that''s dangerous. cool shot though.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-09 01:20:53.</i></td>', 'Nice picture of this hotel (specially compared to some that I saw in that historical link. cool to see it before though). I think one of the big problems of this shot, especially for DPC isn''t extremely interesting to look at...it doesn''t have the DPC "wow" factor. I think it is interesting to look at, especially with the vibrant colors and depth you''ve captured, but it is basically a picture of decaying hotel. I think it''d be cool to see somebody inside it looking around, but maybe that''s dangerous. cool shot though.', '2008-02-09 01:19:55.000000', '2008-02-09 01:20:53.000000', 0),
(4472374, 637415, 57775, '<td valign="top">This is really beautiful, but I think it could be drastically improved by converting it to Black &amp; White.  The color doesn''t really add anything to this photo and is just slightly distracting IMO - it''s all about the wonderful composition, which appears much stronger when you''ve taken out the color.</td>', 'This is really beautiful, but I think it could be drastically improved by converting it to Black & White.  The color doesn''t really add anything to this photo and is just slightly distracting IMO - it''s all about the wonderful composition, which appears much stronger when you''ve taken out the color.', '2008-02-09 01:22:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472422, 640754, 43073, '<td valign="top">This is an astoundingly good image. I keep looking at it and seeing nuances, movement, depth. Shadows that I know were moving are still, those that were still, move. I can''t quite see it all, no matter how much I look, there''s always more, and I can''t stop looking (nor do I want to). Delightful.</td>', 'This is an astoundingly good image. I keep looking at it and seeing nuances, movement, depth. Shadows that I know were moving are still, those that were still, move. I can''t quite see it all, no matter how much I look, there''s always more, and I can''t stop looking (nor do I want to). Delightful.', '2008-02-09 03:03:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472479, 633427, 30982, '<td valign="top">I always figured St Peter would take the whole thing at one time, not just the head.  But it appears you were there at just the right instant as the process began.</td>', 'I always figured St Peter would take the whole thing at one time, not just the head.  But it appears you were there at just the right instant as the process began.', '2008-02-09 04:23:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472481, 639950, 78196, '<td valign="top">Lovely winter image. I get the feeling that a bit too much USM has gone into the branches (though I could be wrong) which takes away from their delicate nature somewhat. I''m wondering if you burned the sky at the top of the image, as it seems a little unnaturally grey - although this could be highlighted by USM on the brances. The image is a busy one; perhaps you could have focused a little more on the path or the house, as currently the voters'' eyes aren''t drawn to either.</td>', 'Lovely winter image. I get the feeling that a bit too much USM has gone into the branches (though I could be wrong) which takes away from their delicate nature somewhat. I''m wondering if you burned the sky at the top of the image, as it seems a little unnaturally grey - although this could be highlighted by USM on the brances. The image is a busy one; perhaps you could have focused a little more on the path or the house, as currently the voters'' eyes aren''t drawn to either.', '2008-02-09 04:28:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472482, 640430, 78196, '<td valign="top">I love this. I don''t suppose you were expecting this to score highly, but it''s a great find and the processing is absolutely spot-on. I wonder if you could have introduced a little more contrast into the TV screen to highlight the reflection - I think this was missed by a lot of voters.</td>', 'I love this. I don''t suppose you were expecting this to score highly, but it''s a great find and the processing is absolutely spot-on. I wonder if you could have introduced a little more contrast into the TV screen to highlight the reflection - I think this was missed by a lot of voters.', '2008-02-09 04:31:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472483, 640756, 78196, '<td valign="top">Nice shot and composition, though I think I''d prefer the bird even closer to the bottom left of the frame - personal thing.  Again, this is one of those shots which is neither sharp not intentionally blurry. If the shutter were a little longer on this you''d have captured the bird''s energy wonderfully, though probably scoring lower in the process. But hey, who cares about votes, right? There''s some haloing around the subject that is possibly only visible on my (rubbish) laptop screen, but a bit of careful burning can make that disappear. More USM on the bird would sharpen things up again but increase the haloing. Perhaps you could have been more daring with the contrast in the sky as well... just a thought. But well seen and captured, and a photo I like very much.</td>', 'Nice shot and composition, though I think I''d prefer the bird even closer to the bottom left of the frame - personal thing.  Again, this is one of those shots which is neither sharp not intentionally blurry. If the shutter were a little longer on this you''d have captured the bird''s energy wonderfully, though probably scoring lower in the process. But hey, who cares about votes, right? There''s some haloing around the subject that is possibly only visible on my (rubbish) laptop screen, but a bit of careful burning can make that disappear. More USM on the bird would sharpen things up again but increase the haloing. Perhaps you could have been more daring with the contrast in the sky as well... just a thought. But well seen and captured, and a photo I like very much.', '2008-02-09 04:35:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472487, 640943, 78196, '<td valign="top">The pose of the bird really gives it character, and the negative space is great. I''m a little perturbed by the sloped dark background, which I think draws the attention away from the bird a little, but nevertheless a great quirky shot which I like very much.</td>', 'The pose of the bird really gives it character, and the negative space is great. I''m a little perturbed by the sloped dark background, which I think draws the attention away from the bird a little, but nevertheless a great quirky shot which I like very much.', '2008-02-09 04:38:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472490, 640534, 78196, '<td valign="top">Nicely processed. I assume this is HDR or at least with shadow/highlight adjustment? The light and colours is excellent and this is reflected in the high score. If anything it''s the lack of a single identifiable subject that hurts this (the mast isn''t strong enough as an anchor point) as our eyes are wandering all over the image.</td>', 'Nicely processed. I assume this is HDR or at least with shadow/highlight adjustment? The light and colours is excellent and this is reflected in the high score. If anything it''s the lack of a single identifiable subject that hurts this (the mast isn''t strong enough as an anchor point) as our eyes are wandering all over the image.', '2008-02-09 04:42:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472491, 628573, 78196, '<td valign="top">Great sky, but I''m finding the clouds lacking in focus and clarity - I don''t know whether this is down to the original image or the quality of the conversion. I wonder if it''s even necessary to have some land towards the bottom - it''s easily missable and looks more like an afterthought - I''d say you could do with a little more. This would help draw our attention to the sunset itself, which is the main focal point of the image anyway. You''d lose some of that amazing sky, of course, but with a wider lens you''d be able to keep it!</td>', 'Great sky, but I''m finding the clouds lacking in focus and clarity - I don''t know whether this is down to the original image or the quality of the conversion. I wonder if it''s even necessary to have some land towards the bottom - it''s easily missable and looks more like an afterthought - I''d say you could do with a little more. This would help draw our attention to the sunset itself, which is the main focal point of the image anyway. You''d lose some of that amazing sky, of course, but with a wider lens you''d be able to keep it!', '2008-02-09 04:45:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472493, 638112, 78196, '<td valign="top">I was scratching my head trying to work out what you did here - the zoom works very well and the colours are gorgeous. The lack of a single main subject has probably lost you marks, but I prefer the overall effect!</td>', 'I was scratching my head trying to work out what you did here - the zoom works very well and the colours are gorgeous. The lack of a single main subject has probably lost you marks, but I prefer the overall effect!', '2008-02-09 04:48:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472500, 640014, 33352, '<td valign="top">Nice work Roz, so life like..</td>', 'Nice work Roz, so life like..', '2008-02-09 05:04:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472502, 640876, 33352, '<td valign="top">A 9 from me thought this may have finished higher, good result for free study.</td>', 'A 9 from me thought this may have finished higher, good result for free study.', '2008-02-09 05:06:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472506, 638219, 33352, '<td valign="top">A little tounge in cheek with the sign when you consider what your part of the world has been through, good finish.</td>', 'A little tounge in cheek with the sign when you consider what your part of the world has been through, good finish.', '2008-02-09 05:11:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472513, 639803, 33352, '<td valign="top">A lot of good work has been done in this shot to bring in the different greens against the red, my first thought was wrong profile, portrait my have brought you higher scores.</td>', 'A lot of good work has been done in this shot to bring in the different greens against the red, my first thought was wrong profile, portrait my have brought you higher scores.', '2008-02-09 05:17:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472517, 640751, 33352, '<td valign="top">Regardless of the comments, I believe you have done a good job here Shez.</td>', 'Regardless of the comments, I believe you have done a good job here Shez.', '2008-02-09 05:21:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472518, 640430, 65035, '<td valign="top">I love these weird little surreal moments in life and you have captured this beautifully. The dof is just perfect and the muted colours are nice, it would be interesting to see with a more acid look though. I think it''s a great shot but it''s one of those quieter shots that get so easily overlooked on DPC.</td>', 'I love these weird little surreal moments in life and you have captured this beautifully. The dof is just perfect and the muted colours are nice, it would be interesting to see with a more acid look though. I think it''s a great shot but it''s one of those quieter shots that get so easily overlooked on DPC.', '2008-02-09 05:23:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472527, 640756, 65035, '<td valign="top">This is beautiful, the tones are lovely and I love the pattern that the cloudy sky gives the background. It''s a lovely, quiet, peaceful photo. The score you got for this is absurd but that does seem to happen.</td>', 'This is beautiful, the tones are lovely and I love the pattern that the cloudy sky gives the background. It''s a lovely, quiet, peaceful photo. The score you got for this is absurd but that does seem to happen.', '2008-02-09 05:33:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472530, 640943, 65035, '<td valign="top">This is fun, it made me smile as soon as I opened it. I''m in two minds about the dark area of the background, on the one hand it would probably be more DPC friendly without it but for me the image would lose some of it''s impact if you cropped it out. It looks like the duck (goose?) has someplace to go, he looks like he''s checking for traffic before heading for that dark area.</td>', 'This is fun, it made me smile as soon as I opened it. I''m in two minds about the dark area of the background, on the one hand it would probably be more DPC friendly without it but for me the image would lose some of it''s impact if you cropped it out. It looks like the duck (goose?) has someplace to go, he looks like he''s checking for traffic before heading for that dark area.', '2008-02-09 05:40:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472534, 640534, 65035, '<td valign="top">Oooo I love the beach when it''s moody and wild and you''ve captured that beautifully. As to why it didn''t score higher, well it <i>is</i> DPC you shoulda put a naked girl on one of those boats. :P</td>', 'Oooo I love the beach when it''s moody and wild and you''ve captured that beautifully. As to why it didn''t score higher, well it is DPC you shoulda put a naked girl on one of those boats. :P', '2008-02-09 05:47:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472535, 638112, 65035, '<td valign="top">Wow! Jelena this is beautiful! The colours are gorgeous and the zoom is very clever. I don''t know why it didn''t score higher, sometimes I just don''t understand. :(</td>', 'Wow! Jelena this is beautiful! The colours are gorgeous and the zoom is very clever. I don''t know why it didn''t score higher, sometimes I just don''t understand. :(', '2008-02-09 05:53:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472545, 634259, 78110, '<td valign="top">this pics should get better place!!</td>', 'this pics should get better place!!', '2008-02-09 06:09:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472562, 640398, 90084, '<td valign="top">I think this is a spectacular photo.  It is truly breathtaking!</td>', 'I think this is a spectacular photo.  It is truly breathtaking!', '2008-02-09 06:44:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472568, 640852, 90084, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous!</td>', 'Gorgeous!', '2008-02-09 06:46:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472585, 640347, 47378, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote in this challenge, but this one should have scored a little higher. It''s a great shot, and she''s beautiful! Definitely a shot to be proud of.</td>', 'I didn''t vote in this challenge, but this one should have scored a little higher. It''s a great shot, and she''s beautiful! Definitely a shot to be proud of.', '2008-02-09 06:57:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472593, 638977, 32345, '<td valign="top">This is a very good family portrait and it deserved a much better score. I think that the grain killed it.</td>', 'This is a very good family portrait and it deserved a much better score. I think that the grain killed it.', '2008-02-09 07:14:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472594, 638581, 32345, '<td valign="top">This is a very good B&amp;W street picture, I think that the blur person in the foreground killed it.</td>', 'This is a very good B&W street picture, I think that the blur person in the foreground killed it.', '2008-02-09 07:15:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472595, 640693, 32345, '<td valign="top">I think that you were robbed on this. I really love this high key picture.</td>', 'I think that you were robbed on this. I really love this high key picture.', '2008-02-09 07:19:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472597, 635468, 47483, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NikonJeb:</b></div><hr/><i> LOL!!! I''m probably not the right person to evaluate this image....mine:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=640942" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/640942.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/640942.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/797/120/640942.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I love the composition, not so much the color/tone processing. I''d love to see this in a low or no-sat version. It should have done better IMO. It is a lovely, peaceful setting. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I do value your comment a lot.</td>', 'Originally posted by NikonJeb: LOL!!! I''m probably not the right person to evaluate this image....mine:  I love the composition, not so much the color/tone processing. I''d love to see this in a low or no-sat version. It should have done better IMO. It is a lovely, peaceful setting.   I do value your comment a lot.', '2008-02-09 07:23:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472598, 635468, 47483, '<td valign="top">The dark version was my original vision about this photo. This is what I saw one I shot it. <br/>I asked my brother to stop car and jumped out of it and took three pics. It was so surreal, these white birds flocking this tree while the day was dying, right there in front of me. <br/> <br/>For the pastles version, I guess time to time painter in me comes out and I try to have party with colors. This is one good thing about being hobby photographer.</td>', 'The dark version was my original vision about this photo. This is what I saw one I shot it. I asked my brother to stop car and jumped out of it and took three pics. It was so surreal, these white birds flocking this tree while the day was dying, right there in front of me.  For the pastles version, I guess time to time painter in me comes out and I try to have party with colors. This is one good thing about being hobby photographer.', '2008-02-09 07:26:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472695, 628573, 43073, '<td valign="top">As I see this, three worlds are coming together, about to merge. One is water and land, grounded and solid; the next stormy, dynamic, unpredictable; and the final is blue and white, peaceful, genteel even; only with the storm can the lighter than air blues be merged with the solids below, only with the storm can the three parts become a whole. And you''ve captured it . . . wonderful.</td>', 'As I see this, three worlds are coming together, about to merge. One is water and land, grounded and solid; the next stormy, dynamic, unpredictable; and the final is blue and white, peaceful, genteel even; only with the storm can the lighter than air blues be merged with the solids below, only with the storm can the three parts become a whole. And you''ve captured it . . . wonderful.', '2008-02-09 08:46:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472718, 640673, 18080, '<td valign="top">stunning</td>', 'stunning', '2008-02-09 09:03:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472728, 640943, 43073, '<td valign="top">You''ve shot the beastie from the back: how dare you! There aren''t pretty colors throughout: how dare you! The horizon is *gasp* tilted!  How dare you! I love this, not because there are technical "faults," not even "in spite of" the "faults", but simply because I find it intriguing, and all the elements together -- darkness, light, processing, composition -- heighten that intrigue for me. I''m glad you shot and processed as you did.</td>', 'You''ve shot the beastie from the back: how dare you! There aren''t pretty colors throughout: how dare you! The horizon is *gasp* tilted!  How dare you! I love this, not because there are technical "faults," not even "in spite of" the "faults", but simply because I find it intriguing, and all the elements together -- darkness, light, processing, composition -- heighten that intrigue for me. I''m glad you shot and processed as you did.', '2008-02-09 09:11:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472761, 640756, 32786, '<td valign="top">I like the negative space When I first looked at it for some reason I was thinking it would look better if the bird was in the corner I see someone else thought the same. I really like how the sky looks. I also like the sepia look you choose gives ia a kind of timeless look. not sure but maybe you could of got a little more detail out of the wing feathers with some more dodging but then again I see that  you probally did that already.</td>', 'I like the negative space When I first looked at it for some reason I was thinking it would look better if the bird was in the corner I see someone else thought the same. I really like how the sky looks. I also like the sepia look you choose gives ia a kind of timeless look. not sure but maybe you could of got a little more detail out of the wing feathers with some more dodging but then again I see that  you probally did that already.', '2008-02-09 09:49:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472803, 635468, 62787, '<td valign="top">Wow, that is beautiful! An intense burst of colour that hits you and makes you jump as soon as you look at it... The title is most appropriate, to me this is like visual poetry. And who cares about the score, I''d be happy to see this on my wall any day.</td>', 'Wow, that is beautiful! An intense burst of colour that hits you and makes you jump as soon as you look at it... The title is most appropriate, to me this is like visual poetry. And who cares about the score, I''d be happy to see this on my wall any day.', '2008-02-09 10:13:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472808, 640637, 30850, '<td valign="top">I had given this a 6.  Two changes that might have improved the shot are:<br/> <br/>A slightly higher crop on the bottom - perhaps to just below the bolt on the bumper.  The undercarriage and sky showing under there are a bit distracting.<br/> <br/>The hotspot reflections on the grill are a bit strong.  You might have changed the angle of the shoot slightly or toned them down in post processing.</td>', 'I had given this a 6.  Two changes that might have improved the shot are: A slightly higher crop on the bottom - perhaps to just below the bolt on the bumper.  The undercarriage and sky showing under there are a bit distracting. The hotspot reflections on the grill are a bit strong.  You might have changed the angle of the shoot slightly or toned them down in post processing.', '2008-02-09 10:15:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472815, 638112, 43073, '<td valign="top">Stunning. You''ve captured the ether; are the gods aware? They''re not going to be very happy, you know. First you capture fire, over and over again; then beauty is captured of you by firelight; and, then this: the ephemeral, caught, trapped, allowing those of us who are unable to see it with our souls to see it with our eyes. Yes, I might be drawn deeper in if the tree on top was dark black, pure shadow against the soft skeins of color in the ''tweens, but it is quite lovely as is.<br/></td>', 'Stunning. You''ve captured the ether; are the gods aware? They''re not going to be very happy, you know. First you capture fire, over and over again; then beauty is captured of you by firelight; and, then this: the ephemeral, caught, trapped, allowing those of us who are unable to see it with our souls to see it with our eyes. Yes, I might be drawn deeper in if the tree on top was dark black, pure shadow against the soft skeins of color in the ''tweens, but it is quite lovely as is.', '2008-02-09 10:17:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472845, 640852, 28029, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot, Neil. Congratulations on the ribbon.</td>', 'Beautiful shot, Neil. Congratulations on the ribbon.', '2008-02-09 10:46:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472850, 637756, 35804, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by macrothing:</b></div><hr/><i> <i>Is</i> it a vase?  Or some type of strange multiple exposure photographic trickery?  I didn''t get to this while voting.  It''s interesting - sure looks like you got a kick out of it (good for you). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is a vase...I actually picked it up at TJMaxx believe it or not. Sometimes they get some really cool stuff. I did get a kick out of this for sure.</td>', 'Originally posted by macrothing: Is it a vase?  Or some type of strange multiple exposure photographic trickery?  I didn''t get to this while voting.  It''s interesting - sure looks like you got a kick out of it (good for you).   It is a vase...I actually picked it up at TJMaxx believe it or not. Sometimes they get some really cool stuff. I did get a kick out of this for sure.', '2008-02-09 10:50:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472870, 640430, 62787, '<td valign="top">What really makes this shot for me is the reflection in the TV. The image itself is on a small, limited space, but then you sneakily manage to get what''s basically a vanishing point into one of the reflections :)<br/> <br/>The light is pretty cool too - I like the outline of light framing the chair. And the DOF works for me. The retro processing feel is very cool too. Damn you for lack of sexy models and northern lights though, whatever were you thinking :p<br/> <br/></td>', 'What really makes this shot for me is the reflection in the TV. The image itself is on a small, limited space, but then you sneakily manage to get what''s basically a vanishing point into one of the reflections :) The light is pretty cool too - I like the outline of light framing the chair. And the DOF works for me. The retro processing feel is very cool too. Damn you for lack of sexy models and northern lights though, whatever were you thinking :p ', '2008-02-09 11:20:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472876, 640756, 62787, '<td valign="top">I love the expanding sense of possibilities present in this picture. It''s something about the way the bird is going upwards. And you''re right, detail shouldn''t be required to appreciate the message of this... To me, what the bird is saying is: "I am alone. And I am free. I''m a master of my own destiny. And there''s an expanse of sky ahead, to fly through as I choose, as far as my wings will carry me." <br/>The simplicity of the image makes the message both clear and powerful.</td>', 'I love the expanding sense of possibilities present in this picture. It''s something about the way the bird is going upwards. And you''re right, detail shouldn''t be required to appreciate the message of this... To me, what the bird is saying is: "I am alone. And I am free. I''m a master of my own destiny. And there''s an expanse of sky ahead, to fly through as I choose, as far as my wings will carry me." The simplicity of the image makes the message both clear and powerful.', '2008-02-09 11:27:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472881, 640943, 62787, '<td valign="top">I love this. You''ve captured a moment. The birdie seems deep in thought, sort of distractedly walking along while its mind is elsewhere. And oddly, I can very much identify with the mood. So the level of personification present in the picture very much impresses me - it''s not often you see a picture that seems to express an animal''s emotional state :)</td>', 'I love this. You''ve captured a moment. The birdie seems deep in thought, sort of distractedly walking along while its mind is elsewhere. And oddly, I can very much identify with the mood. So the level of personification present in the picture very much impresses me - it''s not often you see a picture that seems to express an animal''s emotional state :)', '2008-02-09 11:32:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4472904, 635266, 68980, '<td valign="top">freakin awesome. i love it. fantastic perspective :)</td>', 'freakin awesome. i love it. fantastic perspective :)', '2008-02-09 11:48:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473006, 640774, 66267, '<td valign="top">I love minimalism! A way underrated shot.</td>', 'I love minimalism! A way underrated shot.', '2008-02-09 13:14:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473016, 638137, 59029, '<td valign="top">Terrific leading lines and comp and dof - what more is there to say? Definitely worthy of the blue!</td>', 'Terrific leading lines and comp and dof - what more is there to say? Definitely worthy of the blue!', '2008-02-09 13:27:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473079, 638112, 83313, '<td valign="top">Surprised this only did a 5.8, but freestudies are really hard on scoring. This is great. I love the effect.</td>', 'Surprised this only did a 5.8, but freestudies are really hard on scoring. This is great. I love the effect.', '2008-02-09 14:21:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473085, 639327, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like the more contrasty version you linked to a little better. Not fond of the subject being so centered, though.</td>', 'I like the more contrasty version you linked to a little better. Not fond of the subject being so centered, though.', '2008-02-09 14:27:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473090, 639721, 83313, '<td valign="top">I didn''t think the combination of sepia and strong colors would do well overall, though I liked it''s use here. Sometimes you know it will not appeal to the broad spectrum of tastes. This one was an experiment in a way. <br/> <br/>Sometimes you just need to throw it against the wall and see if it sticks. (Or is that "Run it up the flagpole and see who salutes"?)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-09 14:32:17.</i></td>', 'I didn''t think the combination of sepia and strong colors would do well overall, though I liked it''s use here. Sometimes you know it will not appeal to the broad spectrum of tastes. This one was an experiment in a way.  Sometimes you just need to throw it against the wall and see if it sticks. (Or is that "Run it up the flagpole and see who salutes"?)', '2008-02-09 14:31:09.000000', '2008-02-09 14:32:17.000000', 0),
(4473164, 637756, 39850, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RKT:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by macrothing:</b></div><hr/><i> <i>Is</i> it a vase?  Or some type of strange multiple exposure photographic trickery?  I didn''t get to this while voting.  It''s interesting - sure looks like you got a kick out of it (good for you). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is a vase...I actually picked it up at TJMaxx believe it or not. Sometimes they get some really cool stuff. I did get a kick out of this for sure. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Bet it looks ''unique'' full of flowers.  And ah, that is the tv (was trying to work it out).. going to look at the ''giffy'' now.</td>', 'Originally posted by RKT: Originally posted by macrothing: Is it a vase?  Or some type of strange multiple exposure photographic trickery?  I didn''t get to this while voting.  It''s interesting - sure looks like you got a kick out of it (good for you).   It is a vase...I actually picked it up at TJMaxx believe it or not. Sometimes they get some really cool stuff. I did get a kick out of this for sure.   Bet it looks ''unique'' full of flowers.  And ah, that is the tv (was trying to work it out).. going to look at the ''giffy'' now.', '2008-02-09 15:26:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473350, 640398, 24962, '<td valign="top">Larus, there is nothing I can add, except you SUCK!! :))) No you don''t! I can''t add any comments other than, breathtaking beauty shot of your world. A surreal, sharp, crisp photo that has everyone on DPC drooling!<br/> <br/>You are one kewl Dude!</td>', 'Larus, there is nothing I can add, except you SUCK!! :))) No you don''t! I can''t add any comments other than, breathtaking beauty shot of your world. A surreal, sharp, crisp photo that has everyone on DPC drooling! You are one kewl Dude!', '2008-02-09 16:44:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473372, 639803, 43073, '<td valign="top">There is a definite softness here, not in processing, not in "focus" but in feel. It moves me across the image, but always brings me back.  It''s quite delightful, and I bet would make an awesome print.</td>', 'There is a definite softness here, not in processing, not in "focus" but in feel. It moves me across the image, but always brings me back.  It''s quite delightful, and I bet would make an awesome print.', '2008-02-09 16:50:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473432, 637992, 30982, '<td valign="top">What I like best about this is the sorta gawky pre-adolescent nature of the beastie - kinda knock-knee''d, a little awkward, and has that baby fur growing out thing going on.  I have no problem with the snow - looks like snow to me.</td>', 'What I like best about this is the sorta gawky pre-adolescent nature of the beastie - kinda knock-knee''d, a little awkward, and has that baby fur growing out thing going on.  I have no problem with the snow - looks like snow to me.', '2008-02-09 17:11:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473522, 638759, 80087, '<td valign="top">How did I miss this????? I like it and I think you are crazy!!! Love ya<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-09 17:44:06.</i></td>', 'How did I miss this????? I like it and I think you are crazy!!! Love ya', '2008-02-09 17:41:43.000000', '2008-02-09 17:44:06.000000', 0),
(4473555, 640182, 65083, '<td valign="top">You come to the table with such awesome photos.  I admire the work that you do, it makes me want to work harder to learn.</td>', 'You come to the table with such awesome photos.  I admire the work that you do, it makes me want to work harder to learn.', '2008-02-09 18:18:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473556, 639803, 65083, '<td valign="top">Deb you are another one that brings awesome shots to the table each and every challenge.  You make me want to work and learn more.</td>', 'Deb you are another one that brings awesome shots to the table each and every challenge.  You make me want to work and learn more.', '2008-02-09 18:21:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473580, 632908, 78196, '<td valign="top">I appreciate your frustration with this one - this shot clearly speaks to you a lot but the voters just see an OOF figurine and click the ''tank'' button. It will have been the shutter speed that has caused this - I never shoot under 1/80 on my 50mm with my slightly shaky hands! As has been mentioned before, the border, though it works well with the colour scheme, is a bit too garish for most tastes (including mine if I''m honest). The important thing is that you keep submitting what means the most to you. With a bit of luck, someone else will feel the same way!</td>', 'I appreciate your frustration with this one - this shot clearly speaks to you a lot but the voters just see an OOF figurine and click the ''tank'' button. It will have been the shutter speed that has caused this - I never shoot under 1/80 on my 50mm with my slightly shaky hands! As has been mentioned before, the border, though it works well with the colour scheme, is a bit too garish for most tastes (including mine if I''m honest). The important thing is that you keep submitting what means the most to you. With a bit of luck, someone else will feel the same way!', '2008-02-09 18:44:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473587, 640231, 78196, '<td valign="top">I really like the processing on this. I think the reasons for the low-ish score have been pretty much covered, but well done for submitting something a little different.</td>', 'I really like the processing on this. I think the reasons for the low-ish score have been pretty much covered, but well done for submitting something a little different.', '2008-02-09 18:46:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473600, 638823, 78196, '<td valign="top">For each of these photos I''ve commented on, I''ve loaded the photo and tried to guess the score. 9 out of 10 times I''m pretty much spot on, but here I was miles out. I just don''t understand the score. The IR is subtle and the conversion superb. The DoF is done to absolute perfection. And it really is dance-like. Somehow. Wonderful shot and I''d just ignore the voters!</td>', 'For each of these photos I''ve commented on, I''ve loaded the photo and tried to guess the score. 9 out of 10 times I''m pretty much spot on, but here I was miles out. I just don''t understand the score. The IR is subtle and the conversion superb. The DoF is done to absolute perfection. And it really is dance-like. Somehow. Wonderful shot and I''d just ignore the voters!', '2008-02-09 18:51:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473610, 640401, 78196, '<td valign="top">IMO this shot doesn''t benefit at all from the B&amp;W conversion, as the nature of the lighting is pretty flat - not a criticism as it works perfectly well in the colour version. The blown out hair is also much more incongruous in the B&amp;W context. On a personal level I don''t get particularly excited by photos of model-like women, no matter how beautiful, if I don''t feel any kind of emotional connection with the subject. Her expression here doesn''t speak to me, but this is obviously incredibly subjective. That''s my two cents anyway! :)</td>', 'IMO this shot doesn''t benefit at all from the B&W conversion, as the nature of the lighting is pretty flat - not a criticism as it works perfectly well in the colour version. The blown out hair is also much more incongruous in the B&W context. On a personal level I don''t get particularly excited by photos of model-like women, no matter how beautiful, if I don''t feel any kind of emotional connection with the subject. Her expression here doesn''t speak to me, but this is obviously incredibly subjective. That''s my two cents anyway! :)', '2008-02-09 18:56:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473615, 634908, 78196, '<td valign="top">At first I wondered whether the goat was really in focus - I think it is but it really needs to pop out at us a little bit more (some USM would do the trick if applied well) and the image is a little bit lacking in contrast. It would make a terrific B&amp;W I reckon (in fact, if you''d like me to have a play then do send me over a larger version though I can''t claim to be an expert!). You''ve captured real energy here and the bokeh is nice too :)</td>', 'At first I wondered whether the goat was really in focus - I think it is but it really needs to pop out at us a little bit more (some USM would do the trick if applied well) and the image is a little bit lacking in contrast. It would make a terrific B&W I reckon (in fact, if you''d like me to have a play then do send me over a larger version though I can''t claim to be an expert!). You''ve captured real energy here and the bokeh is nice too :)', '2008-02-09 18:59:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473643, 640667, 7743, '<td valign="top">Yellow and red are probably the hardest colours to portray in an image.  I think this image suffers from being too bright therefore causing the colours to block up a lot.  To achieve more detail in the flowers it would need to be exposed less.  You may be able to adjust this in your photo editor.  Best bet is to try and shoot again.</td>', 'Yellow and red are probably the hardest colours to portray in an image.  I think this image suffers from being too bright therefore causing the colours to block up a lot.  To achieve more detail in the flowers it would need to be exposed less.  You may be able to adjust this in your photo editor.  Best bet is to try and shoot again.', '2008-02-09 19:22:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473732, 640222, 61651, '<td valign="top">This is very lovely - I like the square crop you chose for this.</td>', 'This is very lovely - I like the square crop you chose for this.', '2008-02-09 20:09:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473738, 640651, 68178, '<td valign="top">Good textures and geometry. Not sure how you could improve it... I also agree that it would very likely do better in a more specific challenge. It just doesn''t jump out at you in a free study.</td>', 'Good textures and geometry. Not sure how you could improve it... I also agree that it would very likely do better in a more specific challenge. It just doesn''t jump out at you in a free study.', '2008-02-09 20:12:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473740, 640970, 61651, '<td valign="top">Oh, that score is criminal.  Makes me almost sorry I bugged you to enter it. Almost. :)  I like it very much, and hope you didn''t sweat the votes too badly.</td>', 'Oh, that score is criminal.  Makes me almost sorry I bugged you to enter it. Almost. :)  I like it very much, and hope you didn''t sweat the votes too badly.', '2008-02-09 20:12:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473750, 639803, 61651, '<td valign="top">I like the softness you got here.  The non-standard composition - lordy, you even have them going right to left! - really makes this a compelling image to look at.  One of my 9s.</td>', 'I like the softness you got here.  The non-standard composition - lordy, you even have them going right to left! - really makes this a compelling image to look at.  One of my 9s.', '2008-02-09 20:16:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473753, 637992, 61651, '<td valign="top">I can''t get any more articulate than this: awwwwwwwwwwww...   :)</td>', 'I can''t get any more articulate than this: awwwwwwwwwwww...   :)', '2008-02-09 20:18:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473756, 638552, 68178, '<td valign="top">I think this should have scored better. I think the colors, DOF, and bokeh are spot on. Not sure it would be possible but if you could have composed it with the two reds at opposite points of the thirds, it might have helped the flow of the picture. That said, I would have voted it a 7 had I voted.</td>', 'I think this should have scored better. I think the colors, DOF, and bokeh are spot on. Not sure it would be possible but if you could have composed it with the two reds at opposite points of the thirds, it might have helped the flow of the picture. That said, I would have voted it a 7 had I voted.', '2008-02-09 20:19:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473774, 629830, 61651, '<td valign="top">I thought this was just lovely - the toning especially is a nice touch.  And I like the perspective that wide angle affords - you really get a sense of the immense height of these trees.</td>', 'I thought this was just lovely - the toning especially is a nice touch.  And I like the perspective that wide angle affords - you really get a sense of the immense height of these trees.', '2008-02-09 20:32:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473776, 640759, 61651, '<td valign="top">Figured this would be an above-6. :)  Great job on this, really solid focus.</td>', 'Figured this would be an above-6. :)  Great job on this, really solid focus.', '2008-02-09 20:33:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473778, 640852, 4793, '<td valign="top">A beautiful shot/Congratulations</td>', 'A beautiful shot/Congratulations', '2008-02-09 20:35:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473785, 635266, 61651, '<td valign="top">One of those shots that I just had to look up afterward to hopefully find out how the heck you got it.  I am very impressed!</td>', 'One of those shots that I just had to look up afterward to hopefully find out how the heck you got it.  I am very impressed!', '2008-02-09 20:39:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473788, 637468, 61651, '<td valign="top">Thought this was superb, one of my 10s - great B&amp;W conversion.</td>', 'Thought this was superb, one of my 10s - great B&W conversion.', '2008-02-09 20:42:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473791, 640857, 61651, '<td valign="top">There''s just something about frogs...really enjoy looking at this.  Simple composition, nicely done.</td>', 'There''s just something about frogs...really enjoy looking at this.  Simple composition, nicely done.', '2008-02-09 20:43:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473793, 639334, 61651, '<td valign="top">A cat photo to beat the band - really good, gets across the personality of this particular cat very well.</td>', 'A cat photo to beat the band - really good, gets across the personality of this particular cat very well.', '2008-02-09 20:45:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473798, 637756, 61651, '<td valign="top">That is one HELL of a vase.  Really liked the surreality of this, gave it an 8.</td>', 'That is one HELL of a vase.  Really liked the surreality of this, gave it an 8.', '2008-02-09 20:48:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473800, 640603, 61651, '<td valign="top">I really liked this, and I can''t tell you why, either. :)</td>', 'I really liked this, and I can''t tell you why, either. :)', '2008-02-09 20:49:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473808, 640759, 51538, '<td valign="top">Nicely done.  English robins have a certain panache that their North American counterparts do not.  Yours is a nice composition.</td>', 'Nicely done.  English robins have a certain panache that their North American counterparts do not.  Yours is a nice composition.', '2008-02-09 20:57:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473810, 639334, 51538, '<td valign="top">What a nice Sunday morning feeling in your photo.  You captured not only a fine visual image but also an invisible emotion.  Well done.</td>', 'What a nice Sunday morning feeling in your photo.  You captured not only a fine visual image but also an invisible emotion.  Well done.', '2008-02-09 20:59:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473823, 637756, 51538, '<td valign="top">I recently sold (stupidly sold) a pair of brass tragedy and comedy masks, antiques.  They had plenty of useful emotion related to daily life in God''s Country.  So I have been looking high and low to find a replacement set of masks - but all I seem to find are these multi-faced brass Buddhas...  Your prop is perfect, invaluable.  Oh yes, the message is spot on as well.  I look out  in Brooklyn and all the windows have that eerie blue glow of TV screens...  Lucky don''t have one here and never had one when growing up so avoided that habit at least...</td>', 'I recently sold (stupidly sold) a pair of brass tragedy and comedy masks, antiques.  They had plenty of useful emotion related to daily life in God''s Country.  So I have been looking high and low to find a replacement set of masks - but all I seem to find are these multi-faced brass Buddhas...  Your prop is perfect, invaluable.  Oh yes, the message is spot on as well.  I look out  in Brooklyn and all the windows have that eerie blue glow of TV screens...  Lucky don''t have one here and never had one when growing up so avoided that habit at least...', '2008-02-09 21:06:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473834, 639950, 61651, '<td valign="top">This is a pretty scene, and that dirt path gives us a bit of a respite from all the white, and leads the eye to the background too.  Overall, though I don''t get a strong sense of subject, and that might have been what a lot of other voters felt too.</td>', 'This is a pretty scene, and that dirt path gives us a bit of a respite from all the white, and leads the eye to the background too.  Overall, though I don''t get a strong sense of subject, and that might have been what a lot of other voters felt too.', '2008-02-09 21:12:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4473975, 640398, 66597, '<td valign="top">Larus, I think this may be my favorite of all your northern lights shots. I really like the way the road is offset by the large green area. Provides an interesting balance. I saw your post above about possibly putting them together for an exhibition and/or book. A grand idea.</td>', 'Larus, I think this may be my favorite of all your northern lights shots. I really like the way the road is offset by the large green area. Provides an interesting balance. I saw your post above about possibly putting them together for an exhibition and/or book. A grand idea.', '2008-02-09 22:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474160, 633017, 56539, '<td valign="top">Excellent photo as usual and my vote of 10, as usual!</td>', 'Excellent photo as usual and my vote of 10, as usual!', '2008-02-09 23:53:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474189, 640943, 68504, '<td valign="top">Sharp focus on Goosey, billtip to webtoe and the ground whereon he stands against the blurred bg, and the wonderful definition within his whites delightfully emphasize his quirky random moment in the universe.  (Not to compete with Pineapple or Posthumerus). If I had anything definitive to say about the background I''d be a better photographer than I already am, but looking at your alternate Goosey where the bg is more in focus I am tempted to suspect you might think it provided some of the same context it did there.  But I applaud the negative space.</td>', 'Sharp focus on Goosey, billtip to webtoe and the ground whereon he stands against the blurred bg, and the wonderful definition within his whites delightfully emphasize his quirky random moment in the universe.  (Not to compete with Pineapple or Posthumerus). If I had anything definitive to say about the background I''d be a better photographer than I already am, but looking at your alternate Goosey where the bg is more in focus I am tempted to suspect you might think it provided some of the same context it did there.  But I applaud the negative space.', '2008-02-10 00:01:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474259, 638581, 30982, '<td valign="top">Too busy for DPC and the kind of shot I LOVE to take.  Light here is also the kind of light I love to shoot in.  You have very good detail and range throughout which is tough to get in that kind of light.  Had I voted I''d have scored this fairly high, but that''s because it is indeed my kind of shot.  The average voter probably didn''t much care for the whole "too much" thing, nor the guy on the right of the frame.</td>', 'Too busy for DPC and the kind of shot I LOVE to take.  Light here is also the kind of light I love to shoot in.  You have very good detail and range throughout which is tough to get in that kind of light.  Had I voted I''d have scored this fairly high, but that''s because it is indeed my kind of shot.  The average voter probably didn''t much care for the whole "too much" thing, nor the guy on the right of the frame.', '2008-02-10 00:33:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474268, 640430, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is just fine as it is.  I think the beauty of these after-challenge discussions is it allows viewers to linger a bit more with shots they may have missed during voting, to appreciate the more subtle and often far better entries that get "lost" in the split-second voting process.  Nostalgic and sad - strong combination created by your image.  And a wee bit quirky, too.  I love the cobweb on the fence.</td>', 'This is just fine as it is.  I think the beauty of these after-challenge discussions is it allows viewers to linger a bit more with shots they may have missed during voting, to appreciate the more subtle and often far better entries that get "lost" in the split-second voting process.  Nostalgic and sad - strong combination created by your image.  And a wee bit quirky, too.  I love the cobweb on the fence.', '2008-02-10 00:38:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474273, 640534, 30982, '<td valign="top">The ocean is the most perfect color in this.  Nice muted palette of colors, too.  Wee bit of color noise (from HDR or shadows/highlights, maybe?) in the clouds that may have distracted a few picky voters.</td>', 'The ocean is the most perfect color in this.  Nice muted palette of colors, too.  Wee bit of color noise (from HDR or shadows/highlights, maybe?) in the clouds that may have distracted a few picky voters.', '2008-02-10 00:41:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474277, 639334, 48928, '<td valign="top">The story behind this is right on par with the photo.  I love cats and this captures so much that I love about them, thanks for sharing!<br/> <br/></td>', 'The story behind this is right on par with the photo.  I love cats and this captures so much that I love about them, thanks for sharing! ', '2008-02-10 00:43:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474287, 640819, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful image - I''m quite taken by it.  I love the grays, the ripples, the solitary nature of the tree as it stands guard day in and day out.  Well seen, well photographed.</td>', 'This is a beautiful image - I''m quite taken by it.  I love the grays, the ripples, the solitary nature of the tree as it stands guard day in and day out.  Well seen, well photographed.', '2008-02-10 00:50:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474299, 638823, 30982, '<td valign="top">As I''d commented on some of your other IR shots, I usually don''t care for IR, but I like what you''re doing with it and the fact it doesn''t scream IR.  It''s very subtle, very quiet, and has a sort of ethereal feel to it.  This is a lovely study of shapes, curves, light.  Very well titled, too!</td>', 'As I''d commented on some of your other IR shots, I usually don''t care for IR, but I like what you''re doing with it and the fact it doesn''t scream IR.  It''s very subtle, very quiet, and has a sort of ethereal feel to it.  This is a lovely study of shapes, curves, light.  Very well titled, too!', '2008-02-10 00:55:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474303, 640035, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh!  Reminds me of the signs like "Beer Ice Dancing" you see on little joints on the sides of back roads.  I actually like the busy-ness of this - definitely adds to the cluttered and disorganized feel of the place.</td>', 'Heh!  Reminds me of the signs like "Beer Ice Dancing" you see on little joints on the sides of back roads.  I actually like the busy-ness of this - definitely adds to the cluttered and disorganized feel of the place.', '2008-02-10 00:59:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474306, 640756, 30982, '<td valign="top">You see isolation, I see grace and elegance and the beauty of form.  Purposefulness, even.  Tones are lovely and that splash of cloud adds a lovely depth and texture.</td>', 'You see isolation, I see grace and elegance and the beauty of form.  Purposefulness, even.  Tones are lovely and that splash of cloud adds a lovely depth and texture.', '2008-02-10 01:02:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474308, 640854, 30982, '<td valign="top">Excellent timing and worth the stalking of the poor thing.  :-)  I love the trio of the bird, the reflection, and the shadow, all showing the bird''s form in different ways.</td>', 'Excellent timing and worth the stalking of the poor thing.  :-)  I love the trio of the bird, the reflection, and the shadow, all showing the bird''s form in different ways.', '2008-02-10 01:06:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474312, 640943, 30982, '<td valign="top">This gives me the sense of a performer of some kind, about to take the stage or enter the arena.  Also begs the question of why just the one?  I quite like the shot.</td>', 'This gives me the sense of a performer of some kind, about to take the stage or enter the arena.  Also begs the question of why just the one?  I quite like the shot.', '2008-02-10 01:10:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474333, 638112, 30982, '<td valign="top">Amazing effect and a very interesting perspective on a sunset!  The whole of the world reaches up to the grandeur that is the sky, knowing full well they can never touch it, but to not try is unthinkable.</td>', 'Amazing effect and a very interesting perspective on a sunset!  The whole of the world reaches up to the grandeur that is the sky, knowing full well they can never touch it, but to not try is unthinkable.', '2008-02-10 01:29:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474338, 635000, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''m liking the B&amp;W stuff!  This definitely has a presence to it - imposing as you say in your title.</td>', 'I''m liking the B&W stuff!  This definitely has a presence to it - imposing as you say in your title.', '2008-02-10 01:31:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474340, 639950, 30982, '<td valign="top">To me the subject is the scene itself and the marvelous quiet that envelops when snow is falling.  And the fact I can see snow falling.</td>', 'To me the subject is the scene itself and the marvelous quiet that envelops when snow is falling.  And the fact I can see snow falling.', '2008-02-10 01:32:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474591, 640014, 39110, '<td valign="top">Woohoo Roz fanatstic result for you and your excellent skills ;)</td>', 'Woohoo Roz fanatstic result for you and your excellent skills ;)', '2008-02-10 04:46:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474608, 629050, 60173, '<td valign="top">That looks like such a fun parade! The costumes are fantastic. You captured the vivid colors well. Those bright colors are so easily over exposed.<br/> <br/>It looks like you were in a shaded area, so my suggestion for next time might be to bump up your ISO a bit so that you can use a faster shutter speed. Paraders do a lot of waving and their costumes generally have a lot of moving pieces. I think that movement blur really had a negative impact on the shot.<br/> <br/>Composition wise, it''s a candid so several rules are often forgivable, but there''s still the basics to keep in mind to make the image powerful. If you look at your rule of thirds you have the tail end of a car and the subject''s wave, your subject, and then the next row of paraders. The tail end of the car cheapens the shot. I know, I know.. cars are big part of parades, but I find it distracting for this shot. It takes away from the parader''s wave, which should be the main action of the shot.<br/> <br/>I think your final score may have been lower than if you had entered this into more of a themed challenge. Freestudies are tough.</td>', 'That looks like such a fun parade! The costumes are fantastic. You captured the vivid colors well. Those bright colors are so easily over exposed. It looks like you were in a shaded area, so my suggestion for next time might be to bump up your ISO a bit so that you can use a faster shutter speed. Paraders do a lot of waving and their costumes generally have a lot of moving pieces. I think that movement blur really had a negative impact on the shot. Composition wise, it''s a candid so several rules are often forgivable, but there''s still the basics to keep in mind to make the image powerful. If you look at your rule of thirds you have the tail end of a car and the subject''s wave, your subject, and then the next row of paraders. The tail end of the car cheapens the shot. I know, I know.. cars are big part of parades, but I find it distracting for this shot. It takes away from the parader''s wave, which should be the main action of the shot. I think your final score may have been lower than if you had entered this into more of a themed challenge. Freestudies are tough.', '2008-02-10 05:39:38.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4474639, 639327, 60173, '<td valign="top">This one really is a mystery. I''m sure by now you know your candids are under appreciated, but quality wise it''s no lesser quality than your higher scoring ones. I don''t think that elbow in the shot should have knocked you so low, so I wonder if it''s the actual subject that people didn''t like.<br/> <br/>I remember seeing this during the voting and asking myself "how does he know he''s a pimp?" At the time I didn''t know it was your photo, although I should have since it screams Pawdrix. Since I didn''t know it was you I thought the photographer was just stereotyping this guy and had I voted, it may have had an effect on the score. To most of the world pimps are just something we see in the movies.<br/> <br/>If this photo were on a themed website that was documenting New York streets it would seem less out of place. In the DPC environment it seems like a photo of a snappy dresser being labeled as a pimp. <br/> <br/>With that all said it''s a very interesting photo. People always seem so relaxed and natural in your photos. These are definitely not people you''d see walking down Oregon streets, heh.</td>', 'This one really is a mystery. I''m sure by now you know your candids are under appreciated, but quality wise it''s no lesser quality than your higher scoring ones. I don''t think that elbow in the shot should have knocked you so low, so I wonder if it''s the actual subject that people didn''t like. I remember seeing this during the voting and asking myself "how does he know he''s a pimp?" At the time I didn''t know it was your photo, although I should have since it screams Pawdrix. Since I didn''t know it was you I thought the photographer was just stereotyping this guy and had I voted, it may have had an effect on the score. To most of the world pimps are just something we see in the movies. If this photo were on a themed website that was documenting New York streets it would seem less out of place. In the DPC environment it seems like a photo of a snappy dresser being labeled as a pimp.  With that all said it''s a very interesting photo. People always seem so relaxed and natural in your photos. These are definitely not people you''d see walking down Oregon streets, heh.', '2008-02-10 06:25:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474647, 640398, 31533, '<td valign="top">Wow, I for one cannot get enough of these borealis shots.<br/>I''m trying to convince my wife to go to Iceland for a holiday.<br/>Congrats with the ribbon !</td>', 'Wow, I for one cannot get enough of these borealis shots.I''m trying to convince my wife to go to Iceland for a holiday.Congrats with the ribbon !', '2008-02-10 06:44:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474655, 635468, 60173, '<td valign="top">I remember seeing this during the challenge and thinking to myself "wow.. that''s not going to do well." I almost instantly appreciated the beauty of the photo though. It is very Impressionistic. <br/> <br/>You''re photo quite clearly belongs on a wall. It is very much a painting. Unfortunately, the voters on DPC don''t usually appreciate photos that aren''t perfectly crisp with a clear subject and colors they expect to see. <br/> <br/>In your own words you were "trying something different." In looking at other photos in your profile, I can tell you that you don''t need my advice on how to take a photo. I think this photo was just an experiment that isn''t appreciated by the masses in this venue. If it were a painting on a wall in a museum the opinions would be vastly different. Keep experimenting. You''re a great photographer!</td>', 'I remember seeing this during the challenge and thinking to myself "wow.. that''s not going to do well." I almost instantly appreciated the beauty of the photo though. It is very Impressionistic.  You''re photo quite clearly belongs on a wall. It is very much a painting. Unfortunately, the voters on DPC don''t usually appreciate photos that aren''t perfectly crisp with a clear subject and colors they expect to see.  In your own words you were "trying something different." In looking at other photos in your profile, I can tell you that you don''t need my advice on how to take a photo. I think this photo was just an experiment that isn''t appreciated by the masses in this venue. If it were a painting on a wall in a museum the opinions would be vastly different. Keep experimenting. You''re a great photographer!', '2008-02-10 07:00:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474665, 640942, 60173, '<td valign="top">I had to look around the results of this photo to try and understand why it placed where it did. It really didn''t deserve a 5.3, but there''s some great photos that placed above it. There''s some not-so-great ones up there too, but they''re the typical DPC crowd pleasers to which I say "eh..."<br/> <br/>This is an absolutely beautiful scene. If the foreground tree wasn''t where it is, I''d have no qualms with the composition, but as it is, I want to push it out of the way. <br/> <br/>Your processing does seem a bit rough. You say there was "minimal doinking," but it looks over sharpened. I love the colors though. One thing I noticed was a pale pink in the background along the water line. If you could bring that out a touch, I think it would add greatly to the whole image.<br/> <br/>Overall this is a great winter image that is very telling of the area you live. There is a lot of great elements. If I had voted I would have given it no less than a 7. Knock out the tree and give me some pink and it would have been a 9.</td>', 'I had to look around the results of this photo to try and understand why it placed where it did. It really didn''t deserve a 5.3, but there''s some great photos that placed above it. There''s some not-so-great ones up there too, but they''re the typical DPC crowd pleasers to which I say "eh..." This is an absolutely beautiful scene. If the foreground tree wasn''t where it is, I''d have no qualms with the composition, but as it is, I want to push it out of the way.  Your processing does seem a bit rough. You say there was "minimal doinking," but it looks over sharpened. I love the colors though. One thing I noticed was a pale pink in the background along the water line. If you could bring that out a touch, I think it would add greatly to the whole image. Overall this is a great winter image that is very telling of the area you live. There is a lot of great elements. If I had voted I would have given it no less than a 7. Knock out the tree and give me some pink and it would have been a 9.', '2008-02-10 07:18:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474781, 640490, 47483, '<td valign="top">I liked tones in it, but because I do not have much understanding of photography it would be difficult to make any helpful comment. It is good photo though.</td>', 'I liked tones in it, but because I do not have much understanding of photography it would be difficult to make any helpful comment. It is good photo though.', '2008-02-10 08:46:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474783, 631978, 47483, '<td valign="top">OOOOOOOO, the blur has killed it. Could have been a good photo but the blur. I am not sure if it was intensional but it does not gel well with DPC crowd.</td>', 'OOOOOOOO, the blur has killed it. Could have been a good photo but the blur. I am not sure if it was intensional but it does not gel well with DPC crowd.', '2008-02-10 08:48:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474785, 640693, 47483, '<td valign="top">Everything in this photo is very good. Strong and a meaningful composition. Liked it.</td>', 'Everything in this photo is very good. Strong and a meaningful composition. Liked it.', '2008-02-10 08:49:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474787, 633148, 47483, '<td valign="top">you are one of my fav photog on this site. Its a pleasure to look at what you bring. I did not vote in this challenge but it would have been one of my highest votes. Do not wish to change anything in it.</td>', 'you are one of my fav photog on this site. Its a pleasure to look at what you bring. I did not vote in this challenge but it would have been one of my highest votes. Do not wish to change anything in it.', '2008-02-10 08:51:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474791, 637396, 47483, '<td valign="top">This is something difficult to shoot. And you have captured it very well.</td>', 'This is something difficult to shoot. And you have captured it very well.', '2008-02-10 08:53:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474795, 640059, 47483, '<td valign="top">I have so so feeling for it. Liked it but I would not jump out of my chair with WOW. I think you entered what you liked and not what could have scored well. You surely know how to score well.</td>', 'I have so so feeling for it. Liked it but I would not jump out of my chair with WOW. I think you entered what you liked and not what could have scored well. You surely know how to score well.', '2008-02-10 08:55:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4474983, 640553, 52945, '<td valign="top">Excellent self-portrait, you have amazing eyes. The hat works very well and I like the blurred hair in the background.</td>', 'Excellent self-portrait, you have amazing eyes. The hat works very well and I like the blurred hair in the background.', '2008-02-10 10:40:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4475038, 640398, 90097, '<td valign="top">This is no doubt a fantastic picture.<br/>Keep up the good work.</td>', 'This is no doubt a fantastic picture.Keep up the good work.', '2008-02-10 11:08:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4475324, 633017, 88523, '<td valign="top">Truly awesome...read your bio on your profile...amazing how in a given moment a stranger could have such a positive impact on another.</td>', 'Truly awesome...read your bio on your profile...amazing how in a given moment a stranger could have such a positive impact on another.', '2008-02-10 14:10:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4475329, 632908, 54843, '<td valign="top">Julianne - I''m not sure I can add any more than what has already been said below. I can understand if this image speaks to you, as I have a few that speak to me but nobody else.  Unfortunately, this never translates into a matching score.  If you want a better score, reference the below technical comments...but if you are happy with it and I think you are...be proud of it and ignore the narrow opinions that are the majority of DPC voting.</td>', 'Julianne - I''m not sure I can add any more than what has already been said below. I can understand if this image speaks to you, as I have a few that speak to me but nobody else.  Unfortunately, this never translates into a matching score.  If you want a better score, reference the below technical comments...but if you are happy with it and I think you are...be proud of it and ignore the narrow opinions that are the majority of DPC voting.', '2008-02-10 14:14:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4475344, 640231, 54843, '<td valign="top">I think this image had great potential.  I like the subject and the girl is very cute...so I don''t think that was the real problem. I would like to see the colors improved a little (mentioned below).  I am also left wanting a little more sharpness. Lastly, I think if you had just inched over a little to your left the composition would have benefited...I just would like to see a little more of the tattooing.</td>', 'I think this image had great potential.  I like the subject and the girl is very cute...so I don''t think that was the real problem. I would like to see the colors improved a little (mentioned below).  I am also left wanting a little more sharpness. Lastly, I think if you had just inched over a little to your left the composition would have benefited...I just would like to see a little more of the tattooing.', '2008-02-10 14:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4475353, 638823, 54843, '<td valign="top">This shot strikes me right away as "elegant" and didn''t even come across as IR until I read that from your comments.  Everyone seems a little stumped as to how to help on this one.  I can''t really say I can help either.  Perhaps this is because the issue is with your composition, yet the subject itself is very difficult to compose and no one can really visualize how to adjust your camera position.  My suggestion is to go back to the plant and move around your camera until you find a nice composition that makes a lot of leading lines and diagonals...this should produce a similar shot that will speak more strongly to viewers.<br/> <br/>I hope this helps.</td>', 'This shot strikes me right away as "elegant" and didn''t even come across as IR until I read that from your comments.  Everyone seems a little stumped as to how to help on this one.  I can''t really say I can help either.  Perhaps this is because the issue is with your composition, yet the subject itself is very difficult to compose and no one can really visualize how to adjust your camera position.  My suggestion is to go back to the plant and move around your camera until you find a nice composition that makes a lot of leading lines and diagonals...this should produce a similar shot that will speak more strongly to viewers. I hope this helps.', '2008-02-10 14:33:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4475476, 638137, 79531, '<td valign="top">nice work!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-10 15:48:21.</i></td>', 'nice work!', '2008-02-10 15:46:47.000000', '2008-02-10 15:48:21.000000', 0),
(4475597, 638137, 89957, '<td valign="top">this  is beauiftul</td>', 'this  is beauiftul', '2008-02-10 16:48:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4475599, 640398, 89957, '<td valign="top">wow</td>', 'wow', '2008-02-10 16:48:57.000000', NULL, 0),
