(4477500, 633427, 32767, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> "... it''s just too Ed Clarke<br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//blackyak.com/dpc/yellowpost.jpg'', strrpos(''//blackyak.com/dpc/yellowpost.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//blackyak.com/dpc/yellowpost.jpg"/> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Too Ed Clarke? Impossible! Bite your tongue.<br/> <br/>There''s never enough Ed.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-11 09:29:48.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: "... it''s just too Ed Clarke   Too Ed Clarke? Impossible! Bite your tongue. There''s never enough Ed.', '2008-02-11 09:29:13.000000', '2008-02-11 09:29:48.000000', 0),
(4477820, 632908, 68256, '<td valign="top">Julianne, my initial reaction when I saw this was the grain and the border destroyed it.  You said in your comments "lighting, composition, and focus are decent.." I think people are expecting the technicals to be perfect rather than decent in a free study (for good or bad...).  I gave it a 4 during voting mainly because I had no "connection" with the subject conbined with the "decent" but not perfect technicals.  I also agree with most of what has been said below.</td>', 'Julianne, my initial reaction when I saw this was the grain and the border destroyed it.  You said in your comments "lighting, composition, and focus are decent.." I think people are expecting the technicals to be perfect rather than decent in a free study (for good or bad...).  I gave it a 4 during voting mainly because I had no "connection" with the subject conbined with the "decent" but not perfect technicals.  I also agree with most of what has been said below.', '2008-02-11 11:03:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4477840, 640231, 68256, '<td valign="top">I like this composition with the diagonal arm adding some tension and the diagonal line in the background.  I think the processing is fine and the lighting is good.  For some reason I don''t feel "involved" in the scene though..perhaps because the girls expression is so "hum drum".  I think it is the small things that brought this photo down to its score..the flourescent light, and the tatooers OOF back of head.  Also keep in mind that this is a free study so the voting can be harsher.  This had the capability to score in the 6s in a themed challenge in my opinion.</td>', 'I like this composition with the diagonal arm adding some tension and the diagonal line in the background.  I think the processing is fine and the lighting is good.  For some reason I don''t feel "involved" in the scene though..perhaps because the girls expression is so "hum drum".  I think it is the small things that brought this photo down to its score..the flourescent light, and the tatooers OOF back of head.  Also keep in mind that this is a free study so the voting can be harsher.  This had the capability to score in the 6s in a themed challenge in my opinion.', '2008-02-11 11:10:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4477852, 638823, 68256, '<td valign="top">I just noticed that this finished 1 place in front of mine!  I think one problem with the shot (and it is a lovely shot!) is the in focus leaf tips kinda take the viewer away from the berries.  The shallow DOF works fine for me, but only if there aren''t random other spots in focus...</td>', 'I just noticed that this finished 1 place in front of mine!  I think one problem with the shot (and it is a lovely shot!) is the in focus leaf tips kinda take the viewer away from the berries.  The shallow DOF works fine for me, but only if there aren''t random other spots in focus...', '2008-02-11 11:15:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4477865, 640401, 68256, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot and gave it an 8 during voting.  The stare works so well and I don''t mind the blown out hair at all.  I actually do prefer the original color version and would have probably given it a 9 though.  I love dramatic lights comeing from odd locations as your seperation light is...just suites my taste I guess.  I really am shocked this didn''t score at least a 6....strange!</td>', 'I really like this shot and gave it an 8 during voting.  The stare works so well and I don''t mind the blown out hair at all.  I actually do prefer the original color version and would have probably given it a 9 though.  I love dramatic lights comeing from odd locations as your seperation light is...just suites my taste I guess.  I really am shocked this didn''t score at least a 6....strange!', '2008-02-11 11:19:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4477876, 634908, 68256, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6 during voting and I really liked the strong diagonal composition.  A little more seperation from the background and a little more contrast in the hair (as figaro mentioned) and I would have voted higher.  It is really shocking how high the standards are with wildlife photography here at DPC...5.2 certainly isn''t a reflection of the quality of this shot.</td>', 'I gave this a 6 during voting and I really liked the strong diagonal composition.  A little more seperation from the background and a little more contrast in the hair (as figaro mentioned) and I would have voted higher.  It is really shocking how high the standards are with wildlife photography here at DPC...5.2 certainly isn''t a reflection of the quality of this shot.', '2008-02-11 11:24:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4477887, 638112, 68256, '<td valign="top">This photo doesn''t really work for me personally, but I gave it a 7 during voting because it is well composed, technically good and creative.  Actually I love the effect from the horizon up (just considering the trees), it was the buildings and tree on the bottom that made me dizzy.  Great tones and colors too.</td>', 'This photo doesn''t really work for me personally, but I gave it a 7 during voting because it is well composed, technically good and creative.  Actually I love the effect from the horizon up (just considering the trees), it was the buildings and tree on the bottom that made me dizzy.  Great tones and colors too.', '2008-02-11 11:29:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4477894, 639721, 68256, '<td valign="top">I actually liked this quite a lot and gave it a 7 during voting.  It is definately a strange conversion with the combined saturated sky and desaturated foreground.  I would have given it higher marks if it had been a good old fashion black and white conversion though (especially if the flat lit foreground was dodged and burned to give some texture).<br/> <br/></td>', 'I actually liked this quite a lot and gave it a 7 during voting.  It is definately a strange conversion with the combined saturated sky and desaturated foreground.  I would have given it higher marks if it had been a good old fashion black and white conversion though (especially if the flat lit foreground was dodged and burned to give some texture). ', '2008-02-11 11:33:58.000000', NULL, 0),
