(4480071, 634256, 68178, '<td valign="top">I''ll also echo the DOF sentiment. If the whole main branch was in focus I think it would help. Also you might try to isolate the branch and highlight it in some way (maybe even lighten it up, or burn the background bokeh. That said the composition and colors are good. I probably would have voted this a 6 as is.</td>', 'I''ll also echo the DOF sentiment. If the whole main branch was in focus I think it would help. Also you might try to isolate the branch and highlight it in some way (maybe even lighten it up, or burn the background bokeh. That said the composition and colors are good. I probably would have voted this a 6 as is.', '2008-02-12 08:58:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4480115, 640398, 14591, '<td valign="top">Isn''t it cold in Iceland?   Then why do the people have skin so thin that unless you fawn over a photograph, they have to reply for the 100th time that "I really don''t care."?   Doesn''t criticism help build a person?   I love this site, the photographers (including Larus) found here have some incredible talent, my fav bar none is DrAchoo.   Yet everytime somebody posts anything other than incredible, fantastic, wow, etc...   others have to run to the rescue of the fallen photographer.   For the love of everything Holy, they sound like a little league mother protecting their talentless kid.  So send the hate mail, but please let free speech run rampant.<br/>respond with a post or a you can reach me at <br/>kablinki1@yahoo.com<br/>ps if you want to include a photograph, anything with cleavage will be much appreciated and of course read first.  hee hee</td>', 'Isn''t it cold in Iceland?   Then why do the people have skin so thin that unless you fawn over a photograph, they have to reply for the 100th time that "I really don''t care."?   Doesn''t criticism help build a person?   I love this site, the photographers (including Larus) found here have some incredible talent, my fav bar none is DrAchoo.   Yet everytime somebody posts anything other than incredible, fantastic, wow, etc...   others have to run to the rescue of the fallen photographer.   For the love of everything Holy, they sound like a little league mother protecting their talentless kid.  So send the hate mail, but please let free speech run rampant.respond with a post or a you can reach me at kablinki1@yahoo.comps if you want to include a photograph, anything with cleavage will be much appreciated and of course read first.  hee hee', '2008-02-12 09:29:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4480303, 638137, 89692, '<td valign="top">This is a really strong and emotive photo.  Simply breathtaking and well and truly worthy of the blue prize!</td>', 'This is a really strong and emotive photo.  Simply breathtaking and well and truly worthy of the blue prize!', '2008-02-12 11:15:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4480372, 640651, 54778, '<td valign="top">The texture of the wood really pops out and contrasts well with the white. And it''s a strong geometric shape.. <br/>It''s a simple picture and that''s its strength and weakness.. This was limited scorewise definitely because of the competition typical for free studies ..</td>', 'The texture of the wood really pops out and contrasts well with the white. And it''s a strong geometric shape.. It''s a simple picture and that''s its strength and weakness.. This was limited scorewise definitely because of the competition typical for free studies ..', '2008-02-12 11:57:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4480380, 638552, 54778, '<td valign="top">The image is very pretty.. The colours and composition work really well.. While the dof makes the picture it could also be letting it down a little.. The berries are just not tack sharp dpc style and that makes the viewer feel that it''s slightly oof.. Also I would have liked the two branches to be positioned in the frame slighly apart..</td>', 'The image is very pretty.. The colours and composition work really well.. While the dof makes the picture it could also be letting it down a little.. The berries are just not tack sharp dpc style and that makes the viewer feel that it''s slightly oof.. Also I would have liked the two branches to be positioned in the frame slighly apart..', '2008-02-12 12:03:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4480384, 640872, 54778, '<td valign="top">I like the swirly, darker clouds.. they add something for me in the picture.. though I wish they were more centered.. They would have become a little like leading lines and enter the viewer in...<br/> <br/>Other then that this is a pretty picture with nice colours.. the scores just show they''re are a lot of pretty pictures around..</td>', 'I like the swirly, darker clouds.. they add something for me in the picture.. though I wish they were more centered.. They would have become a little like leading lines and enter the viewer in... Other then that this is a pretty picture with nice colours.. the scores just show they''re are a lot of pretty pictures around..', '2008-02-12 12:09:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4480395, 639497, 54778, '<td valign="top">This picture seems to not have more of a defined focus point and that is it''s biggest problem... and perhaps not enough contrast in colour..</td>', 'This picture seems to not have more of a defined focus point and that is it''s biggest problem... and perhaps not enough contrast in colour..', '2008-02-12 12:16:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4480404, 634256, 54778, '<td valign="top">I can see that the best focus <i>seems </i>to be at the tip so pulling the composition towards more negative space would have been better..The contrast would have shown the glittery bits of ice better..   The dof causes the rest of the ice seem oof and the eye goes straight to that part rather then what should the focus.. Great find though..</td>', 'I can see that the best focus seems to be at the tip so pulling the composition towards more negative space would have been better..The contrast would have shown the glittery bits of ice better..   The dof causes the rest of the ice seem oof and the eye goes straight to that part rather then what should the focus.. Great find though..', '2008-02-12 12:21:43.000000', NULL, 0),
